// Class 10 English Preloaded NCERT Solutions Data Bundle (All 28 Units)
window.CHAPTERS_DATA = {"1":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch1\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">1</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 1: A Letter to God</h2>\n      <p>G.L. Fuentes — Faith, Irony & Human Kindness — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What did Lencho hope for? Why was a downpour desperately needed for his crops?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Lencho, an industrious peasant whose modest house was the solitary one in the entire valley perched on a low crest, hoped for a good downpour or at least a modest shower for his ripe cornfield dotted with flowers, which promised a bountiful harvest. His family's complete livelihood and sustenance for the entire forthcoming year depended directly upon this rain.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Lencho's hope: Good downpour or shower for ripe cornfield</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Significance: Family's sustenance for the entire coming year</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why did Lencho say the raindrops were like 'new coins'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Lencho compared the falling raindrops to 'new coins'—the big drops to ten-cent pieces and the little ones to fives—because rain was the vital catalyst for a rich harvest. Healthy crops would translate directly into prosperity, grain sales, and money in hand. Hence, in his optimistic mind, the falling droplets literally represented incoming coins.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Direct correlation: Rain ensures rich corn harvest -> money & food</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Specific comparison: Big drops = 10-cent pieces, small drops = 5s</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did the rain change? What happened to Lencho's fields?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Sudden Transformation of Rain:</strong><br>Suddenly, a strong wind began to blow, and along with the rain, extraordinarily large hailstones began to fall. The tempest raged furiously for a full hour over the house, the garden, the hillside, and the entire corn valley.</p><p><strong>2. Devastation of the Crops:</strong><br>The field became completely blanketed in white as if salted. Not a single leaf remained on the trees; the corn was utterly demolished, and the blossoms were stripped from the plants, reducing Lencho's hopes to ash.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sudden strong wind and large hailstones falling for an hour</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Total destruction: Field covered like salt, corn destroyed, leaves stripped</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What were Lencho's feelings when the hail stopped?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When the storm subsided, Lencho stood sorrowfully in the middle of his ruined field and told his sons that even a plague of locusts would have left more behind than the hailstorm. His soul was steeped in profound grief and despair, realizing that their year-long toil had produced nothing and that his family would face starvation unless divine intervention occurred.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Locust plague comparison: Storm left less than a swarm of insects</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Deep grief and impending fear of hunger/starvation for the year</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who or what did Lencho have faith in? What did he do?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Lencho had absolute, unquestioning faith in God, whose all-seeing eyes, he had been taught, see everything—even what is deep within one's conscience. Driven by this unflinching conviction, he wrote a letter addressed directly to 'God', detailing that without help his family would go hungry, and demanded 100 pesos to sow his land anew and survive until the next crop arrived.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Unwavering faith in God's omnipresence and divine benevolence</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Action: Wrote letter to 'God' asking for 100 pesos to resow and survive</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who read the letter? What did the postmaster do then?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Letter Received:</strong> The postman first laughed heartily and showed it to his superior; the postmaster—a fat, amiable, and generous gentleman—broke out laughing too, but immediately turned serious, deeply moved by the writer's immense faith.</p><p><strong>2. Postmaster's Noble Gesture:</strong> Determined not to shake Lencho's sublime trust in God, the postmaster decided to reply. Realizing that goodwill alone was insufficient, he contributed a part of his salary, collected donations from his employees and friends as an 'act of charity', and gathered 70 pesos, which he mailed in an envelope signed simply: <em>'God'</em>.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Postmaster read the letter and was inspired by Lencho's unshakeable faith</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Collected 70 pesos from salary and friends as charity; signed as 'God'</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_7\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_7')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q7</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Was Lencho surprised to find a letter with money in it? What made him angry?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Not Surprised:</strong> Lencho showed not the slightest hint of surprise upon opening the envelope containing money; his conviction in God's willingness to help was so total and absolute that he took the arrival of the cash for granted.</p><p><strong>2. Cause of Anger:</strong> When he counted the money, he discovered only 70 pesos instead of the 100 he had requested. Convinced that God could neither make an arithmetic mistake nor deny his plea, he concluded that the post office clerks had stolen the missing 30 pesos.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">No surprise: Absolute certitude of God's response</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Anger: Shortage of 30 pesos; accused post office staff of stealing it</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff1_8\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff1_8')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q8</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who does Lencho think has taken the rest of the money? What is the supreme irony of the ending in 'A Letter to God'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Lencho's Suspicion:</strong><br>Lencho firmly believed that the post office employees had embezzled the missing thirty pesos. In his second letter to God, he pleaded: <em>'Send me the rest, since I need it very much. But don't send it to me through the mail, because the post office employees are a bunch of crooks.'</em></p><p><strong>2. The Supreme Situational Irony:</strong><br>Irony is a literary device where the actual outcome is humorously or tragically opposite to what is expected. In this story:</p><ul><li>The postmaster and postal staff had exhibited extraordinary selflessness, empathy, and sacrifice by parting with their own hard-earned money to preserve a stranger's spiritual faith.</li><li>Instead of receiving gratitude or praise, these very benefactors were branded as a <em>'bunch of crooks'</em> and thieves by the recipient.</li><li>Lencho's blind, naive faith in God made him suspect human goodness, creating a poignant and humorous paradox where noble charity was rewarded with bitter condemnation.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Lencho's belief: Post office employees stole the 30 pesos ('bunch of crooks')</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Definition & demonstration of situational irony: Benefactors labeled thieves</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Critical analysis: Contrast between blind religious faith and human empathy</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 1</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Case Study / Thematic Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Lencho's faith in God was unquestionable, but his faith in humanity was non-existent. How does this story highlight the conflict between faith and practical human understanding?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Lencho possesses a childlike, dogmatic faith in the metaphysical supreme being, believing God actively reads posted mail and sends currency notes. However, he is completely cynical about his fellow humans, immediately assuming the postal workers are dishonest thieves. The story illustrates that while faith gives people the mental fortitude to face disasters, faith without practical discernment can turn into blind delusion and ingratitude. True godliness was actually manifested in the flesh-and-blood postmaster's quiet generosity, which Lencho failed to recognize.</p></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #059669;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#059669;\">Extract-Based Question</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Read the extract and answer: 'What faith! I wish I had the faith of the man who wrote this letter. Starting up a correspondence with God!' (a) Who spoke these words? (b) What action did the speaker take to uphold this faith?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>(a) The postmaster spoke these words to himself upon reading Lencho's first letter addressed to God.<br>(b) To preserve the writer's remarkable faith, the postmaster decided to answer the letter and mobilized his staff, friends, and personal funds to collect 70 pesos to send to Lencho.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <div></div>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(2)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","2":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch2\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">2</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 2: Nelson Mandela: Long Walk to Freedom</h2>\n      <p>Nelson Rolihlahla Mandela — Dignity, Courage & Liberation — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Where did the inauguration ceremony take place? Why is 10 May described as an 'autumn day' in South Africa?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Location:</strong> The historic inauguration ceremonies took place in the Union Buildings amphitheatre in Pretoria, carved out of lovely sandstone, which had been the seat of white supremacy for decades.</p><p><strong>2. 'Autumn Day' in South Africa:</strong> Because South Africa lies in the Southern Hemisphere, its seasonal cycle is opposite to the Northern Hemisphere, making May an autumn month. Metaphorically, autumn signifies harvest and the shedding of old withered leaves—here symbolizing the harvest of South Africa's hard-won freedom and the shedding of centuries of apartheid oppression.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Location: Union Buildings amphitheatre in Pretoria (sandstone structure)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Southern hemisphere autumn season + metaphorical harvest of freedom</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does Mandela mean when he mentions 'an extraordinary human disaster' and 'a glorious human achievement'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. 'Extraordinary Human Disaster':</strong> Mandela refers to the brutal practice of Apartheid—a racially discriminatory system wherein black South Africans were disenfranchised, segregated, dehumanized, and subjected to atrocities on their own land for over three centuries.</p><p><strong>2. 'Glorious Human Achievement':</strong> He refers to the birth of a non-racial, democratic, and egalitarian South African republic where every citizen, regardless of skin color or ethnicity, enjoys equal human dignity, rights, and constitutional liberty.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Disaster: System of Apartheid, racial oppression, segregation</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Achievement: Democratic, non-racial government upholding human rights</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why were two national anthems sung on the day of the inauguration?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Two national anthems were sung to signify the harmonious reconciliation and equality of both races: the whites sang 'Nkosi Sikelel' iAfrika' (God Bless Africa) and the blacks sang 'Die Stem' (The Voice of South Africa), the old republican anthem. Singing both honored the cultural identities of both communities, laying the bedrock of racial unity.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Names of anthems: 'Nkosi Sikelel' iAfrika' (Whites) and 'Die Stem' (Blacks)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Significance: Symbol of racial reconciliation, equality, and unity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How had the attitude of the military generals changed towards Mandela, and why?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The highest military generals and police chiefs, whose chests were decorated with ribbons and medals, saluted Nelson Mandela with solemn allegiance. Mandela recalled with sober irony that not so many years ago, these very generals would not have saluted him but arrested and imprisoned him as a rebel. Their attitude changed because a free, democratic election had legitimately appointed Mandela as the President of South Africa, replacing white supremacy with constitutional democracy.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Contrast: Previously would have arrested him; now saluting in homage</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Reason: Democratic transition, Mandela elected constitutional Commander-in-Chief</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does courage mean to Nelson Mandela? Which does he consider more natural: love or hate?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Meaning of Courage:</strong> Mandela learned that courage was not the absence of fear, but the triumph over it. A brave man is not someone who feels no fear, but one who conquers and overcomes that fear.</p><p><strong>2. Love vs Hate:</strong> Mandela firmly asserts that love comes more naturally to the human heart than its opposite. No one is born hating another person because of skin color, religion, or background; hatred is taught, and if people can learn to hate, they can much more easily be taught to love.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Courage defined: Triumph over fear, not the absence of fear</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Love is natural: Born without hate; love touches human heart organically</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What 'twin obligations' does Mandela mention in the chapter?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Mandela explains that every man in a civil society has twin obligations:</p><ul><li><strong>First Obligation:</strong> To his personal family—parents, wife, and children.</li><li><strong>Second Obligation:</strong> To his larger community, his people, and his country.</li></ul><p>Under the apartheid regime, a man of color attempting to fulfill his duty to his people was ripped from his family and forced to live an isolated life of rebellion and exile.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">First obligation: Personal duties to parents, wife, and children</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Second obligation: Social duties to community, people, and nation</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff2_7\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff2_7')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q7</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Mandela's 'hunger for freedom' change his life? Why does he state that the oppressor must be liberated just as surely as the oppressed?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Transformation from Boyhood to Freedom Fighter:</strong><br>As a boy, Mandela believed he was born free—free to run in the fields, swim in clear streams, and roast mealies under the stars. In youth, he realized these were merely illusions of 'transitory freedoms'. His growing hunger for the real, honorable freedom of his people transformed him completely:</p><ul><li>It turned a frightened young man into a bold revolutionary.</li><li>It drove a law-abiding attorney to become an outlaw living on the run.</li><li>It forced a family-loving husband to live like a monk in prison for 27 years.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Liberation of Both Oppressor and Oppressed:</strong><br>Mandela presents a sublime philosophical insight: <em>'The oppressed and the oppressor alike are robbed of their humanity.'</em> A man who deprives another man of his freedom is himself a prisoner of hatred, locked behind the bars of prejudice and narrow-mindedness. True emancipation requires liberating the oppressed from chains and freeing the oppressor from bigotry.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Evolution of freedom: Boyhood illusions -> adult realization of collective denial</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Personal cost: Law-abiding lawyer to criminal; family man to solitary prisoner</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Philosophy of mutual liberation: Oppressor locked in bigotry, robbed of humanity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 2</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Competency-Based Evaluation</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Mandela observed: 'The depths of oppression create heights of character.' How did the apartheid regime inadvertently produce towering leaders like Oliver Tambo, Walter Sisulu, and Chief Luthuli?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Mandela explains that extreme adversity, systemic cruelty, and ruthless persecution act as a fiery crucible that tempers human willpower. The decades of brutal apartheid oppression demanded extraordinary courage, sacrifice, wisdom, and resilience from resistance leaders, thereby cultivating towering moral giants whose stature might never have been summoned under ordinary conditions. It proved that human spirit shines brightest against the darkest tyranny.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(1)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(3)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","3":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch3\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">3</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 3: Two Stories about Flying</h2>\n      <p>Part I: His First Flight (Liam O'Flaherty) | Part II: Black Aeroplane (Frederick Forsyth)</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff3_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff3_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why was the young seagull afraid to fly? How did his parents and siblings react?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Fear of the Abyss:</strong> The young seagull was paralyzed by terror as he looked down at the vast expanse of sea stretching miles below his high cliff ledge. He felt certain that his slender wings would never support his weight, failing to muster the courage that his younger siblings had shown.</p><p><strong>2. Family's Reaction:</strong> His brothers and little sister, whose wings were shorter than his, had already flown away. His parents flew around him, calling shrilly, scolding him, and threatening to let him starve on his ledge unless he flew away.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fear: High ledge, vast sea below, conviction that wings wouldn't support him</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Family reaction: Scolded, cajoled, threatened with starvation on the ledge</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff3_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff3_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">'The sight of the food maddened him.' What does this suggest? What compelled the young seagull to finally fly?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The young seagull had been starving for twenty-four hours without a crumb. When his mother picked up a piece of fish and flew across towards him, halting just out of reach in mid-air, the excruciating pangs of hunger overcame his crippling terror. Maddened by the sight of food, he uttered a joyful scream and dived recklessly at the fish. As he fell into open space, a monstrous terror seized him for a minute, but immediately his wings spread outward instinctively, catching the air currents, and he was flying.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Extreme hunger (starving for 24h) overpowered his instinctual fear</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mother's clever psychological bait: Diving into space unlocked wings</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff3_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff3_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Describe the young seagull's first flight and his family's exuberant celebration.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">4 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>After his initial dive, the wind rushed against his breast feathers, under his stomach, and against his wings. He realized he was no longer falling headlong; he was soaring gradually downwards and outwards. Flapping his wings, he uttered a joyful cry and soared upwards. When his parents and siblings saw him fly, they flew around him, curvetting, banking, soaring, and diving. When he landed on the green sea, his legs sank into the water and he cried in alarm, but as his belly touched the water, he floated naturally without sinking. His family praised him, screeching happily, and offered him scraps of dog-fish as reward.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sensory sensations of flight: Wind under feathers, graceful soaring</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sea landing: Floating successfully on green water + family offering dog-fish</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff3_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff3_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Part II: 'I'll take the risk.' What was the risk, and why did the narrator of 'The Black Aeroplane' take it?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. The Impending Risk:</strong> The narrator was piloting his old Dakota aeroplane towards England when enormous, mountain-like black storm clouds loomed ahead. His fuel tanks were low, his instruments were fragile, and flying around or over the clouds was impossible.</p><p><strong>2. Reason for Taking Risk:</strong> The narrator took the perilous risk because he was overwhelmingly homesick and longed to be with his family for breakfast, eager to enjoy a wholesome, traditional English morning meal.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Risk: Flying old Dakota with scarce fuel directly into pitch-black storm clouds</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Motivation: Yearning to reach home in England for a hearty family breakfast</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff3_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff3_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Describe the narrator's perilous experience inside the black storm clouds.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Inside the storm, everything was suddenly pitch black; it was impossible to see anything outside the plane. The old Dakota jumped and twisted violently in the turbulent air. When he checked the compass, it was spinning round and round—dead. His radio, altimeter, and other instruments were similarly lifeless. He was lost in the storm without navigation or communication until a mysterious black aeroplane with no lights on its wings appeared alongside him.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Complete blackout; plane violently pitching and twisting</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">All instruments (compass, radio) failed completely; lost in storm</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff3_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff3_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why did the woman in the control center look at the narrator strangely? Who do you think helped the narrator arrive safely?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Why the Woman Looked Strangely:</strong><br>Upon landing safely, the narrator hurried to the control tower to thank the pilot of the black aeroplane who had guided him through the tempest. The woman in the control room laughed with utter astonishment and explained that no other aeroplanes were flying that stormy night; radar showed only his solitary Dakota on the screen.</p><p><strong>2. Critical Analysis of the Mysterious Pilot:</strong><br>The identity of the pilot in the black aeroplane remains an open enigma with two interpretations:</p><ul><li><strong>Psychological / Hallucinatory Reality:</strong> Facing imminent death, the narrator's heightened survival instinct and deep subconscious pilot training manifested as a projection of a guiding plane, keeping his hands steady on the controls.</li><li><strong>Miraculous / Supernatural Providence:</strong> The incident represents an unexplained guardian intervention saving an exhausted flyer in distress.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Control room revelation: Radar detected zero other planes in the stormy sky</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Dual interpretation: Subconscious survival instinct / guardian miracle</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">3 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 3</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">HOTS / Comparative Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Both 'His First Flight' and 'The Black Aeroplane' deal with triumph over fear. Compare the internal mental state of the young seagull with that of the Dakota pilot.</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The young seagull suffered from anticipation terror—the fear of attempting something untried—which was broken only when hunger forced him to take a plunge into the unknown, revealing that his wings were naturally capable. In contrast, the Dakota pilot demonstrated overconfidence bordering on recklessness, entering deadly clouds out of impatience for breakfast, only to be paralyzed by real technological failure. Both stories prove that in moments of extreme peril, the deepest survival instincts within oneself are summoned to conquer fear.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(2)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(4)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","4":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch4\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">4</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 4: From the Diary of Anne Frank</h2>\n      <p>Anne Frank — Adolescence, Wit & Unfiltered Truth — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff4_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff4_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What made writing in a diary a strange experience for Anne Frank? Why did she decide to keep one?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Why Strange:</strong> Writing was a novel experience for thirteen-year-old Anne not only because she had never written anything before, but because she believed that neither she nor anyone else would be interested in the musings of a young schoolgirl.</p><p><strong>2. Why Kept:</strong> Anne felt an urgent emotional need to get things off her chest. She famously remarked that <em>'paper has more patience than people'</em>. Although she had loving parents, an elder sister, and about thirty casual acquaintances, she lacked a true, intimate friend with whom she could confide her deepest feelings.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Novelty of writing + belief that schoolgirl musings wouldn't interest anyone</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Maxim: 'Paper has more patience than people' + lack of a true confidante</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff4_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff4_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why did Anne name her diary 'Kitty'? Why did she give a brief sketch of her family?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Anne named her diary 'Kitty' because she did not want it to be a dry, mechanical ledger of facts; she wanted the diary to be her real, living friend. She provided a brief background of her father Otto Frank, mother Edith, sister Margot, and emigration to Holland because she realized nobody would understand a word of her stories without knowing her background.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Named 'Kitty' to personalize the diary as an intimate, living friend</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Family sketch: Needed context for any future reader to understand her life</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff4_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff4_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What tells you that Anne loved her grandmother deeply?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When Anne's grandmother fell ill in 1941 and had to undergo an operation, Anne worried intensely. After her grandmother's death in January 1942, Anne thought of her constantly and missed her dearly. When Anne's birthday was celebrated later that year, her grandmother's candle was lit alongside the rest, demonstrating her profound, enduring love.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sorrow during illness and persistent affectionate memories after death</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Lit a dedicated candle for grandmother on her 1942 birthday celebration</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff4_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff4_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why was Mr Keesing annoyed with Anne? What punishment essays did he assign to her?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Mr Keesing, the elderly mathematics teacher, was perpetually annoyed with Anne because she was an incorrigible chatterbox who talked incessantly during his lectures. After several warnings failed, he assigned her three punitive essays:</p><ol><li>'A Chatterbox'</li><li>'An Incorrigible Chatterbox'</li><li>'Quack, Quack, Quack, Said Mistress Chatterback'</li></ol>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Reason: Talking excessively during mathematics lessons despite warnings</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Three essay titles correctly enumerated</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff4_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff4_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Anne justify her talkative nature in her first essay?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>In her essay on 'A Chatterbox', Anne argued with brilliant logic that talking was an essential student trait. She explained that while she would try to keep it under control, she could never cure herself of the habit because her mother was just as talkative as she was, if not more so. She humorously pleaded that one cannot do much about inherited traits.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Argument 1: Talking is a natural and vital student characteristic</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Argument 2: Inherited trait from mother; heredity cannot be cured</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff4_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff4_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Anne outsmart Mr Keesing with her third essay? How did Mr Keesing take the joke?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Anne's Ingenious Poetic Verse:</strong><br>When assigned the ridiculous topic <em>'Quack, Quack, Quack, Said Mistress Chatterback'</em>, Anne's friend Sanne, who was good at poetry, helped her write the essay entirely in verse. The poem narrated a satirical story about a mother duck, a father swan, and their three ducklings. The father swan bit his ducklings to death because they quacked too much. The allegory humorously mocked Mr Keesing's intolerance towards innocent schoolgirl chatter.</p><p><strong>2. Mr Keesing's Sporting Response:</strong><br>Mr Keesing appreciated the joke in the right spirit. He read the poem aloud to Anne's class with his own comments and shared it with several other classes. From that day on, Anne was allowed to talk freely in class without receiving extra homework, and Mr Keesing was always making jokes himself.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sanne's help: Wrote poem about father swan biting ducklings for quacking</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Keesing's sporting reaction: Read to class, appreciated wit, stopped punishment</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 4</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Character & Tone Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does Anne's interaction with Mr Keesing demonstrate the power of wit, creative writing, and good humor in resolving classroom friction?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Instead of reacting with sulkiness, defiance, or fear towards her strict teacher, Anne weaponized intellect, humor, and self-deprecating irony. By using logic and verse to defend herself, she turned punishment into literary art. Mr Keesing proved himself to be a humane and enlightened educator by recognizing her talent and sporting spirit rather than taking personal offense, illustrating that gentle humor can dissolve tension far more effectively than authoritarian discipline.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(3)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(5)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","5":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch5\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">5</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 5: Glimpses of India</h2>\n      <p>I. A Baker from Goa | II. Coorg | III. Tea from Assam — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff5_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff5_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Part I: What are the elders in Goa nostalgic about? What was the traditional baker called, and what did he wear?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Nostalgia:</strong> The Goan elders fondly reminisce about the good old Portuguese days and their famous, crusty loaves of bread. While the original Portuguese bakers may have vanished, the mixers, molders, and traditional fiery furnaces still endure.</p><p><strong>2. The Pader & Kabai:</strong> The village baker was known as the <em>'pader'</em>. In the old days, bakers wore a peculiar single-piece long dress reaching down to their knees called the <em>'kabai'</em>. Later in the author's childhood, they wore shirts and trousers shorter than full-length and longer than half-pants.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Nostalgia: Portuguese loaves of bread and traditional wood furnaces</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Baker name: 'Pader'; traditional knee-length attire: 'Kabai'</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff5_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff5_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How were traditional Goan marriages, engagements, and festivals incomplete without bread?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Bread was indispensable to every social occasion in Goan village life:</p><ul><li><strong>Marriage Gifts:</strong> Marriage gifts were meaningless without the sweet bread known as <em>'bol'</em>.</li><li><strong>Engagements:</strong> A daughter's engagement required the mother to prepare special sandwiches.</li><li><strong>Festivals & Christmas:</strong> Cakes and <em>'bolinhas'</em> were an absolute must for Christmas and all major church festivals. A village without a baker's furnace was simply unthinkable.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sweet bread 'bol' essential for marriage gifts</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sandwiches for daughter's engagement</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Cakes and 'bolinhas' mandatory for Christmas & church celebrations</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff5_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff5_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Part II: Where is Coorg situated? What is the story regarding the Greek or Arabic descent of the Kodavus?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Location:</strong> Coorg (Kodagu), Karnataka's smallest district, is nestled midway between coastal Mangalore and Mysore—a piece of heaven of evergreen rainforests, spices, and coffee plantations.</p><p><strong>2. Origin Theories:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Greek Theory:</strong> A part of Alexander the Great's army moved south along the coast and settled there when return became impractical, marrying local women.</li><li><strong>Arabic Theory:</strong> Kodavus wear a traditional long black coat with an embroidered waist-belt known as <em>kuppia</em>, which closely resembles the <em>kuffia</em> worn by Arabs and Kurds.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Location: Midway between Mysore and Mangalore (Karnataka)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Greek descent: Remnants of Alexander's army settled and married locals</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Arabic descent: Traditional coat 'kuppia' resembles Arab 'kuffia'</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff5_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff5_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is the Coorg Regiment famous for? Who was General Cariappa?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The Coorg Regiment is one of the most decorated and valiant regiments in the Indian Army. The very first Chief of the Indian Army, <strong>General Cariappa</strong>, was a proud Coorgi (Kodavu). Furthermore, Kodavus are the only community in India permitted to carry firearms without a license, testifying to their legendary bravery and martial heritage.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Coorg Regiment: One of the most decorated regiments in the Indian Army</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">General Cariappa: First Chief of the Indian Army was a Coorgi</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Unique privilege: Permitted to carry firearms without license</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff5_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff5_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Part III: What are the two legends regarding the discovery of tea described by Rajvir?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Chinese Legend:</strong> An ancient Chinese emperor always boiled water before drinking it. One day, a few twigs of the burning firewood fell into the boiling water, imparting a delightful, invigorating flavor. They were discovered to be tea leaves.</p><p><strong>2. Indian Buddhist Legend:</strong> Bodhidharma, an ancient Buddhist ascetic, cut off his eyelids because he felt drowsy during meditation. Ten tea plants sprouted out of his eyelids. The leaves of these plants, when put into hot water and drunk, banished sleep.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Chinese legend: Twigs accidentally dropped into emperor's boiling water</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Indian Buddhist legend: Bodhidharma's cut eyelids sprouted tea plants</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff5_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff5_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does 'Glimpses of India' celebrate the distinct cultural flavors, traditions, and geography of Goa, Coorg, and Assam?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The three travelogues in 'Glimpses of India' paint a rich, vibrant mosaic of India's cultural and natural heritage:</p><ul><li><strong>Goa (Cultural Continuity):</strong> Highlights the lingering Portuguese influence through the village baker ('pader'). Baking is not merely a commercial trade but a social institution; sweet bread ('bol') and bolinhas are bound to culinary rituals, demonstrating how colonial history blends harmoniously into coastal domestic life.</li><li><strong>Coorg (Martial Honor & Wilderness):</strong> Explores the rugged hills of Kodagu, teeming with coffee aromas, wild elephants, and Mahseer fish in the Kaveri. It celebrates the Kodavus' fierce martial pride, distinct Greek/Arabic ancestry, hospitable traditions, and exceptional bravery.</li><li><strong>Assam (Industrial & Natural Opulence):</strong> Showcases the endless sea of tea bushes across the Brahmaputra valley. It blends historical myths (Bodhidharma and Chinese emperors) with modern botanical knowledge of tea plucking and flushes.</li></ul><p>Together, the chapter fosters deep pride in the kaleidoscope of India's unity in diversity.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Goa: Portuguese baking tradition, pader, social rituals, bol</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Coorg: Martial pride, Kodavus, lush geography, General Cariappa</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Assam: Tea gardens, legends, industrial and economic prominence</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 5</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Competency-Based Evaluation</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Pranjol's father commended Rajvir: 'You seem to have done your homework before coming.' Why is prior research and intellectual curiosity essential when traveling?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Rajvir transformed a routine train journey into an enriching educational experience because he read extensively about tea legends, flushes, and botanical facts before visiting Dhekiabari. While Pranjol took his native tea surroundings for granted, Rajvir observed the pruning, plucking, and seasonal yield with passionate appreciation. Prior research enriches travel, transforming tourists from passive spectators into culturally enlightened observers.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(4)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(6)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","6":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch6\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">6</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 6: Mijbil the Otter</h2>\n      <p>Gavin Maxwell — Human-Animal Companionship & Otter Mischief — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff6_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff6_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What 'experiment' did Maxwell contemplate? Why did he choose an otter instead of a dog?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>After his beloved dog Jonnie died, Maxwell felt heartbroken and unable to endure the pain of having another dog immediately. Since he lived in Camusfearna—a cottage surrounded by water on the Scottish coast—he decided as an experiment to keep an otter instead of a dog, as the watery habitat was ideally suited for a semi-aquatic mammal.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Experiment: Keeping an otter instead of a dog at Camusfearna cottage</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Reason: Grief over dog Jonnie's death + watery location ideal for an otter</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff6_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff6_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Maxwell obtain the otter in Basra? What was its zoological species name?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. How Obtained:</strong> While in Basra collecting his mail from the consulate, Maxwell received a sack delivered by two Arab marsh-dwellers with a note from his friend saying: <em>'Here is your otter...'</em> Inside the squirming sack was an otter cub.</p><p><strong>2. Zoological Classification:</strong> The species was previously unknown to Western science and was later classified by zoologists as <em>Lutrogale perspicillata maxwelli</em>, commonly known as 'Maxwell's otter'.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Delivered by two Arabs in a squirming sack with a note from a friend</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Species name: Lutrogale perspicillata maxwelli (Maxwell's otter)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff6_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff6_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is an otter's characteristic relationship with water? How did Mijbil behave in the bathroom?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>To an otter, static water is an affront to nature; water must be kept on the move, splashed, plunged into, and made to overflow until the bowl or tub is dry. In the bathroom, Mijbil went wild with ecstasy in the bathtub, plunging, rolling, shooting up and down the length of the tub, and making splashes like a hippo. Two days later, he even learned to turn on the water tap with his paws to produce a flow.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Otter trait: Must keep water moving, splashing, and overflowing</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mijbil's bathtub acrobatics and learning to turn on the tap</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff6_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff6_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Describe the traumatic journey of transporting Mijbil inside the box on the aircraft to England.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">4 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. The Box Incident:</strong> The airline insisted that Mijbil be packed in a small box. Before going for a quick meal, Maxwell boxed him. Returning, he found complete silence and blood trickling from the air holes. Mijbil had shredded the zinc lining, cutting himself. Maxwell quickly cleaned the box with ten minutes left for the flight.</p><p><strong>2. Pandemonium on Flight:</strong> Inside the aircraft, Maxwell opened the lid slightly with the airhostess's permission. Mijbil shot out in a flash, disappearing beneath passengers' legs. A woman shrieked: <em>'A rat! A rat!'</em>, standing on her seat. Maxwell dove to catch him and got his face covered in curry. Finally, the kind airhostess helped, and Mijbil returned to sit happily on Maxwell's knees.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Box trauma: Shredded zinc lining, blood trickling, near missed flight</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Aircraft pandemonium: Screaming woman ('A rat!'), curry spill, safe return</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff6_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff6_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What games did Mijbil invent? What were the wild guesses Londoners made about his identity?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">4 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Games Invented:</strong> Mijbil invented a game with a ping-pong ball on Maxwell's sloping suitcase lid. He would place the ball at the high end, run round to the other side, and pounce on it as it rolled down.</p><p><strong>2. Londoners' Wild Guesses:</strong> Londoners had never seen an otter and guessed wildly: a baby seal, a squirrel, a walrus, a beaver, a bear cub, a leopard, a brontosaurus, and even a hippopotamus! The most bizarre guess came from a laborer digging a trench who stared and asked: <em>'Here, mister—what is that supposed to be?'</em></p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Game: Ping-pong ball rolling down sloping suitcase lid</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Wild guesses: Seal, squirrel, walrus, beaver, bear cub, leopard, hippo</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 6</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Value-Based Reflection</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does the story highlight that loving an exotic animal requires immense patience, understanding of its natural instincts, and accommodation?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Gavin Maxwell demonstrates that genuine affection for an animal is not about dominance, but about empathy. He tolerated Mijbil's water splashes, chaotic bathroom rituals, damaged suitcases, and airport panics without anger. He understood that otters are semi-aquatic creatures driven by distinct evolutionary instincts. True pet ownership demands adapting one's lifestyle to the creature's welfare rather than forcing the wild animal to conform to rigid human rules.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(5)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(7)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","7":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch7\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">7</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 7: Madam Rides the Bus</h2>\n      <p>Vallikkannan — Innocence, Curiosity & The Mystery of Death — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff7_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff7_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What was Valli's favorite pastime? What was the source of her unending fascination?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Valli (Valliammai), an eight-year-old girl, had no playmates of her own age on her street. Her favorite pastime was standing in the front doorway of her house, watching what was happening on the street outside. The most fascinating sight of all was the bus that traveled between her village and the nearest town, passing her street every hour with a fresh set of passengers.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Pastime: Standing in front doorway watching street life (no playmates)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fascination: Hourly bus running between village and town with new travelers</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff7_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff7_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Valli gather information and meticulously plan her bus journey?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Valli listened intently to conversations between her neighbors and regular bus travelers, asking discreet questions. She discovered that the town was six miles away, the one-way fare was thirty paise, and the trip took forty-five minutes. She calculated that if she took the one o'clock bus, she would reach town at 1:45 and return home by 2:45, right during her mother's afternoon nap.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Information gathered: 6 miles distance, 30 paise fare, 45 minutes trip</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Planning: Utilizing mother's 1:00 to 2:45 pm afternoon nap time</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff7_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff7_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Valli save up sixty paise for the bus fare? What sacrifices did she make?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Saving sixty paise was an immense feat of self-control for an eight-year-old. Valli painstakingly hoarded every stray stray coin that came her way, ruthlessly stifling every childish urge to buy peppermints, toys, balloons, and sweetmeats. At the village fair, she resisted the supreme temptation of the spinning merry-go-round, keeping her coins safe for the bus ride.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Hoarded every coin; resisted buying peppermints, toys, balloons</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Supreme sacrifice: Resisted merry-go-round at village fair to save 60 paise</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff7_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff7_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why did the bus conductor address Valli as 'Madam'? How did she react?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The bus conductor was a jolly, good-humored fellow. When Valli commanded the bus to stop, refused his hand to help her board, and said with haughty dignity that she could get on by herself with her own thirty paise, the amused conductor bowed politely and teased her by calling her 'Madam'. Valli reacted with sharp indignation, telling him curtly: <em>'I am not a madam!'</em></p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Conductor's joke at Valli's adult-like confidence, dignity, and independence</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Valli's indignant reaction insisting she was not a madam</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff7_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff7_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why didn't Valli get off the bus at the town? Why did she decline the conductor's offer of a cold drink?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Why She Stayed on the Bus:</strong> Valli's sole aim was to experience the bus ride itself. She did not have extra money to spend in the town and had to catch the same bus back before her mother awoke.</p><p><strong>2. Declining Cold Drink:</strong> When the conductor generously offered to buy her a cold drink, Valli politely yet firmly declined, stating that she only had money for her return ticket. This proved her extraordinary self-respect, caution, and discipline.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sole goal was bus experience + lacked extra money and time</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Declining drink demonstrated remarkable self-respect and boundaries</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff7_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff7_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did the sight of the dead cow shatter Valli's joyful enthusiasm? What deeper truth about life and death did she discover?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Joy on Onward Journey:</strong><br>On the way to town, Valli had laughed clapping her hands as a young cow, with its tail held high in the air, galloped frantically right in front of the bus. The more the driver honked, the faster the frightened animal ran, providing immense entertainment.</p><p><strong>2. Tragic Contrast on Return:</strong><br>On the return journey, Valli saw the same cow lying dead by the roadside, struck by a speeding vehicle, its legs stiffened and blood smeared around in a pool. The horrific sight chilled her heart. The creature that had been so full of life, beauty, and energy moments ago had suddenly been converted into a ghastly, lifeless carcass.</p><p><strong>3. Epiphany of Mortality:</strong><br>A profound gloom settled over Valli. She lost all desire to look out the window. The incident marked Valli's awakening to the fragile boundary between life and death. She realized that the adult world contained sudden, irreversible tragedies that childhood innocence cannot foresee.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Contrast: Galloping joyful cow on onward trip vs bloody dead carcass on return</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Psychological impact: Shock, gloom, withdrawal from window view</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Thematic revelation: Child's awakening to the mystery and fragility of mortality</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 7</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Competency-Based Evaluation</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> When Valli returns, her mother remarks: 'So many things in our midst and in the world outside... how can we know about everything?' Valli smiles knowingly. What does Valli's smile signify?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Valli's secret smile signifies her newly acquired maturity and adult perspective. Her mother spoke conceptually about how humans cannot know everything that happens in the world, but Valli had just tasted this reality firsthand through her secret solo adventure. Her smile represents the quiet pride of independence and the bittersweet knowledge of life and death that her mother knew nothing about.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(6)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(8)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","8":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch8\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">8</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 8: The Sermon at Benares</h2>\n      <p>Betty Renshaw — Impermanence, Enlightenment & Transcending Grief — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff8_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff8_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">When and why did Prince Siddhartha Gautama renounce his royal life to seek enlightenment?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>At age twenty-five, while out hunting, Prince Siddhartha was shielded from human suffering by royal luxury. For the first time, he encountered four sights: a sick man, an aged man, a funeral procession, and finally a monk begging for alms. These sights of suffering moved him so deeply that he renounced his palace, wife, and child, wandering for seven years before attaining enlightenment under the Bodhi tree at Bodh Gaya.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Four sights: Sick man, aged man, funeral procession, begging monk</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Transformation: Renounced kingdom, wandered 7 years, achieved enlightenment</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff8_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff8_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Where did Buddha preach his first sermon, and why was this city chosen?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Buddha preached his first sermon at the holy city of Benares (Varanasi), located on the sacred banks of the River Ganges. Benares was chosen because it was the most revered pilgrim center where thousands gathered seeking purification from sin, making it the most fertile ground to spread the noble truths of overcoming death and grief.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">City: Benares (Varanasi) on the banks of River Ganga</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Significance: Foremost sacred pilgrimage center for spiritual awakening</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff8_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff8_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why was Kisa Gotami grieving? What task did the Buddha assign to her?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Grief:</strong> Kisa Gotami was grieving the death of her only son. Paralyzed by grief, she carried the dead child to all her neighbors begging for medicine to bring him back to life.</p><p><strong>2. Buddha's Task:</strong> Buddha asked her to bring him a handful of mustard seeds from a household where no child, husband, parent, or friend had ever died.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Grief: Death of only son; seeking medicine to revive dead child</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Condition: Handful of mustard seeds from a house that had never witnessed death</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff8_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff8_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What realization dawned upon Kisa Gotami when she watched the city lights flicker and extinguish?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Weary and hopeless after finding that every single household had lost a loved one, Kisa Gotami sat down at the wayside watching the lights of the city flicker up and extinguish into darkness. She suddenly realized the universal nature of mortality: human lives flicker up and are extinguished just like lamps. She realized how selfish she had been in her grief, recognizing that death is common to all mortals.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Analogy: City lights flickering up and extinguishing = human lives</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Realization: Selfishness of personal grief; death is universal law for all mortals</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff8_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff8_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">According to the Buddha, how can a mortal overcome sorrow and attain peace of mind? Discuss his earthen vessel analogy.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. The Nature of Mortality:</strong><br>The Buddha taught that the life of mortals in this world is troubled, brief, and combined with pain. Just as ripe fruits are in constant danger of falling, and just as all earthen vessels made by the potter end in being broken, so is the life of mortals subject to death. Neither father nor kinsmen can save anyone from death.</p><p><strong>2. Futility of Weeping:</strong><br>Weeping and grieving cannot restore the dead; instead, lamentation intensifies bodily pain, makes the mourner sick and pale, and torments one's own self without altering reality.</p><p><strong>3. Attaining Peace of Mind:</strong><br>To attain tranquility, a person must extract the arrow of lamentation, complaint, and grief. One who has overcome all sorrow becomes free from sorrow and attains true blessedness (Nirvana).</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Analogies: Ripe fruits falling, earthen pots breaking = certainty of death</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Futility of lamentation: Increases pain, damages body, cannot revive dead</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Prescription for peace: Pull out arrow of grief, embrace detachment</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 8</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Philosophical & Psychological Application</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does Buddha's method of teaching Kisa Gotami prove that experiential learning is far more effective than direct philosophical lecturing?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>If Buddha had directly lectured Kisa Gotami on the inevitability of death, her grief-stricken mind would have rejected his words as cold and unfeeling. By sending her on a personal quest to find a house untouched by death, Buddha allowed her to discover the universal reality through her own interactions. Experiencing the shared grief of dozens of families healed her solipsistic sorrow, proving that self-realization through guided experience is the ultimate pedagogical tool.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(7)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(9)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","9":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch9\" data-book=\"First Flight Prose\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">9</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT PROSE</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 9: The Proposal</h2>\n      <p>Anton Chekhov — Farce, Petty Ego & Mercenary Matrimony — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff9_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff9_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does Chubukov initially suspect Lomov has come for? How does his demeanor change upon learning the true purpose?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When Lomov arrives in formal evening dress with gloves, Chubukov immediately suspects that he has come to borrow money, secretly resolving: <em>'I won't give him any!'</em> However, when Lomov nervously reveals that he has come to ask for his daughter Natalya's hand in marriage, Chubukov is overjoyed. He embraces and kisses Lomov, sheds a happy tear, and enthusiastically blesses the match.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Initial suspicion: Suspected Lomov came to borrow money</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Dramatic change: Overjoyed, kissing and blessing him for marriage proposal</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff9_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff9_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why does Lomov consider Natalya an ideal match for him? What physical ailments torment Lomov?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Practical Match:</strong> Lomov is thirty-five—a critical age—and seeks a quiet, regular domestic life. Natalya is twenty-five, an excellent housekeeper, educated, and not bad-looking, making her an ideal sensible match rather than a romantic passion.</p><p><strong>2. Lomov's Hypochondria:</strong> Lomov suffers from chronic palpitations, insomnia, trembling twitches, high blood pressure, and a jump in his left side whenever he lies down in bed.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Pragmatic reasons: Age 35, good housekeeper, educated, pleasant looks</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Physical ailments: Palpitations, twitching, severe insomnia, panic attacks</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff9_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff9_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does the dispute over Oxen Meadows start and escalate into an ugly fight?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>While preparing to propose, Lomov mentions that his family's Oxen Meadows touch Natalya's birchwoods. Natalya vehemently objects, insisting the Meadows belong to her family. Lomov argues that his aunt's grandmother gave temporary use of the Meadows to Chubukov's grandfather's peasants in exchange for making bricks. The argument degenerates into hysterical screaming, accusations of usurpation, and threats of court action.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Origin: Casual mention of Oxen Meadows ownership touching birchwoods</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Escalation: Brick-making history, calling each other land-grabbers, screaming</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff9_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff9_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Natalya react when she learns that Lomov had come to propose marriage?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When Chubukov insults Lomov and throws him out, he casually mentions that the 'fool' had come to propose to Natalya. The moment Natalya hears this, she falls into hysterical screaming, turns pale, collapses into an armchair, and orders her father: <em>'Bring him back! Bring him here! Ah! Bring him back!'</em> She forgets all territorial pride and desperately demands her suitor's return.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Shock and instant hysterics upon learning of the marriage proposal</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Frantic demand to bring Lomov back immediately, abandoning property fight</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff9_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff9_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What sparks the second bitter quarrel between Lomov and Natalya?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>After Lomov returns, they reconcile over the Meadows, but within minutes enter a second fierce quarrel regarding their hunting dogs. Lomov boasts that his dog <strong>Guess</strong> cost 125 roubles and is first-rate, while Natalya claims her dog <strong>Squeezer</strong>, bought for 85 roubles, is far superior. They insult the pedigree, jaws, and speed of each other's dogs until Lomov collapses unconscious.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Subject: Comparison of hunting dogs (Lomov's Guess vs Natalya's Squeezer)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Escalation: Insulting breeding, overshooting, leading to Lomov's collapse</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"ff9_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('ff9_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How is 'The Proposal' a brilliant satire on 19th-century Russian landowning aristocracy? Describe the farcical climax.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Satire on Commercial Marriage:</strong><br>Chekhov satirizes the mercenary nature of marriage among wealthy Russian landowners. Marriage was viewed not as a sacred emotional union, but as an economic alliance to consolidate estates and wealth. Lomov chooses Natalya out of pragmatic convenience, while Natalya's romantic yearning instantly overrides her moral principles.</p><p><strong>2. Petty Pride and Ego:</strong><br>Despite desperate desire to wed, both characters are hopelessly quarrelsome and vain. Over worthless scraps of marshland ('Oxen Meadows') and dogs ('Guess' vs 'Squeezer'), they exchange venomous personal insults involving ancestors, embezzlements, and lunacy.</p><p><strong>3. Farcical Climax:</strong><br>When Lomov collapses and appears dead, Chubukov panics, fearing a ruined match and police inquiries. When Lomov stirs, Chubukov hurriedly thrusts Natalya's hand into his, shouting: <em>'She's willing! Kiss each other and be damned!'</em> Even while kissing, Natalya immediately reignites the dog argument, shouting: <em>'He's worse!'</em> to which Chubukov shouts: <em>'Champagne! Champagne!'</em> to drown their shouting.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Satire on mercenary marriage alliances in 19th-century Russian aristocracy</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ridiculous pettiness over insignificant property and hunting dogs</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Farcical climax: Forced engagement while shouting insults over champagne</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 9</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Dramatic & Thematic Critique</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Why did Chekhov subtitle 'The Proposal' as 'A Farce'? What elements of farce dominate the play?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>A farce is a comic dramatic work using buffoonery, horseplay, crude characterizations, and ludicrously improbable situations. 'The Proposal' fits this definition completely: exaggerated hypochondria (Lomov trembling, palpitating, collapsing), sudden mood swings (Natalya screaming hysterically to fetch back a man she just called a villain), Chubukov threatening suicide one second and demanding champagne the next, and an engagement sealed amidst screaming arguments.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(8)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(10)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","10":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch10\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">10</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 1: Dust of Snow</h2>\n      <p>Robert Frost — Nature, Mood Transformation & Healing — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">The way a crow\nShook down on me\nThe dust of snow\nFrom a hemlock tree\n\nHas given my heart\nA change of mood\nAnd saved some part\nOf a day I had rued.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Robert Frost</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p1_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p1_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is a 'dust of snow'? What does the poet say has changed his mood?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>A 'dust of snow' refers to the fine, powdery particles or flakes of snow. The sudden, gentle shower of these snow particles shaken down upon the poet by a crow perched on a hemlock tree changed the poet's gloomy, depressed mood into one of sudden joy and freshness.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Definition: Fine powdery snowflakes or particles</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Cause of change: Shower of snow shaken down by crow from hemlock branch</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p1_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p1_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Frost present nature in this poem? What is unusual about his choice of a crow and a hemlock tree?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Unlike traditional Romantic poets who celebrate melodious birds like nightingales or stately trees like oaks and maples, Frost intentionally selects two negative, ill-omened symbols: an ugly, harsh-voiced <strong>crow</strong> and a poisonous <strong>hemlock tree</strong> with white flowers. By using these dark omens to bring about an uplifting, joyful mental rejuvenation, Frost subverts poetic conventions and shows that nature in all its forms has the power to heal.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Unusual symbols: Ill-omened crow and poisonous hemlock tree</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Inversion of convention: Dark symbols become agents of joyful healing</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p1_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p1_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does the poet mean by 'saved some part of a day I had rued'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The word 'rued' means held in regret or sorrow. The poet had spent the earlier part of the day in a somber, despondent frame of mind, feeling that the day was ruined. The unexpected touch of snow broke his depressive reverie, allowing him to appreciate the remaining day with gratitude, thus saving it from being wasted.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Meaning of 'rued': Regretted, spent in melancholy or sorrow</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Saved part: Reclaimed the rest of the day with positivity and cheer</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p1_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p1_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does a seemingly trivial moment in nature have a profound therapeutic impact on the human mind? Analyze the poetic craft of 'Dust of Snow'.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Therapeutic Power of Nature:</strong><br>In 'Dust of Snow', Robert Frost illustrates that human beings often trap themselves in self-created melancholia, sorrow, and trivial anxieties. Nature, through an insignificant micro-event—a crow shaking loose a dusting of snow—startles the poet out of his dark rumination. The cold, crisp sensation reconnects him with the physical universe, shattering his depressive paralysis.</p><p><strong>2. Poetic Craft & Structure:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Conciseness:</strong> Just two stanzas, eight short lines, and twenty-four words capture an entire psychological transformation.</li><li><strong>Rhyme Scheme:</strong> Strict <em>abab cdcd</em> rhyme scheme providing musical harmony.</li><li><strong>Enjambment:</strong> A single continuous sentence running without end-line punctuation until the final full stop, mimicking the swift, uninterrupted flow of emotional renewal.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Therapeutic impact: Breaking depressive paralysis through natural touch</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Subversion of dark omens (crow, hemlock) into agents of light</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Poetic devices: Rhyme scheme abab cdcd, enjambment, brevity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 10</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Extract Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Read the line: 'Has given my heart / A change of mood'. What figure of speech is used in 'Has given my heart', and what does it reveal about the seat of emotions?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The figure of speech is Synecdoche (where a part represents the whole—the 'heart' represents the poet's entire emotional and mental psyche), along with Alliteration in 'Has / Heart'. It reveals that the transformation was not merely superficial or intellectual, but reached the deepest emotional core of his being.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(9)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(11)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","11":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch11\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">11</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 2: Fire and Ice</h2>\n      <p>Robert Frost — Human Passions, Destructive Vices & Apocalyptic Warning — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">Some say the world will end in fire,\nSome say in ice.\nFrom what I've tasted of desire\nI hold with those who favor fire.\n\nBut if it had to perish twice,\nI think I know enough of hate\nTo say that for destruction ice\nIs also great\nAnd would suffice.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Robert Frost</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p2_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p2_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What do 'fire' and 'ice' symbolize in the poem? How do they cause the end of the world?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. 'Fire' Symbolism:</strong> Fire represents unbridled human passions—fiery desire, greed, lust, anger, ambition, and avarice. Like wild fire, unchecked desires spread rapidly, consuming relationships, societies, and resources until the world burns itself out.</p><p><strong>2. 'Ice' Symbolism:</strong> Ice represents cold hatred, indifference, bigotry, rigidity, and cruelty. Unlike the fury of fire, ice destroys quietly by numbing human empathy, freezing warmth and brotherhood until humanity perishes in cold isolation.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fire: Symbol of desire, lust, greed, rage, consuming passions</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ice: Symbol of cold hatred, emotional detachment, intolerance, rigidity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p2_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p2_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why does the poet say he holds with those who favor fire, yet acknowledges ice would also suffice?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The poet aligns himself initially with fire based on his personal life experiences with human desires and burning passions. However, reflecting on human nature, he observes that cold hatred and quiet malice are equally widespread and destructive, concluding that ice is equally potent and sufficient to end civilization.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fire favored due to direct experience of consuming passions/desires</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ice recognized as equally lethal due to deep, silent spread of hatred</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p2_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p2_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is the rhyme scheme of 'Fire and Ice'? How does it unify the poem?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The rhyme scheme of the nine-line poem is <strong>aba abc bcb</strong>. This compact, interlocking rhyme scheme knits the contrasting concepts of fire and ice together, creating a rhythmic inevitability that mirrors the apocalyptic certainty of the world's destruction.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Exact rhyme scheme identified: aba abc bcb</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Function: Interlocking structure linking fiery passion and icy hatred</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p2_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p2_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Robert Frost use cosmological theories to deliver a biting moral critique of human civilization?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Cosmological vs Psychological Destruction:</strong><br>Scientific debates during Frost's era centered on whether the universe would perish through heat death (scorching solar incineration) or cold death (freezing ice age). Frost brilliantly transposes these cosmological theories into psychological metaphors for human moral failings.</p><p><strong>2. Warning Against Self-Destruction:</strong><br>Frost warns that humanity does not require an asteroid or cosmic catastrophe to destroy itself; our own untamed vices are more than adequate. Fiery geopolitical greed causes devastating wars, while cold communal bigotry and indifference rot society from within. The understated, chilling conclusion (<em>'would suffice'</em>) serves as a profound wake-up call to master our passions.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Scientific foundation: Solar heat vs cosmic freeze mapped to moral flaws</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Critique of human vices: Greed/rage (fire) and hatred/indifference (ice)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Understated tone ('would suffice') intensifying dramatic apocalyptic impact</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 11</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Value-Based Application</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> In today's world of climate change and geopolitical conflicts, how is Robert Frost's 'Fire and Ice' exceptionally prophetic?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Frost's poem speaks directly to contemporary crises: environmental destruction and global warming mirror the burning 'fire' of human consumerist greed, while wars, xenophobia, and indifference to suffering mirror the 'ice' of emotional numbness. If humanity fails to temper fiery desires with sustainability and icy prejudices with empathy, our civilization risks fulfilling Frost's apocalyptic prophecy.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(10)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(12)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","12":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch12\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">12</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 3: A Tiger in the Zoo</h2>\n      <p>Leslie Norris — Freedom vs Captivity & The Plight of Caged Wildlife — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">He stalks in his vivid stripes\nThe few steps of his cage,\nOn pads of velvet quiet,\nIn his quiet rage.\n\nHe should be lurking in shadow,\nSliding through long grass\nNear the water hole\nWhere plump deer pass.\n\nHe should be snarling around houses\nAt the jungle’s edge,\nBaring his white fangs, his claws,\nTerrorising the village!\n\nBut he’s locked in a concrete cell,\nHis strength behind bars,\nStalking the length of his cage,\nIgnoring visitors.\n\nHe hears the last voice at night,\nThe patrolling cars,\nAnd stares with his brilliant eyes\nAt the brilliant stars.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Leslie Norris</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p3_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p3_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does the poet contrast the tiger in the zoo with the tiger in its natural habitat?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. In the Zoo:</strong> The tiger is trapped inside a cramped concrete cell. His magnificent strength is locked behind steel bars. He paces the few steps of his cage on velvet pads, helpless, sullen, and ignoring human visitors in silent rage.</p><p><strong>2. In the Wild Jungle:</strong> He should be lurking in the shadows of tall trees, sliding silently through long grass near the water hole to ambush plump deer, and snarling at the forest edge, terrifying villagers with his glistening white fangs and sharp claws.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Zoo: Cramped cell, strength caged, pacing helplessly, ignoring visitors</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Jungle: Lurking in shadows, hunting deer at water hole, snarling with pride</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p3_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p3_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does the poet mean by 'quiet rage'? What literary device is used here?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The phrase 'quiet rage' is an <strong>Oxymoron</strong> (combining contradictory words). The tiger is seething with immense, ferocious fury at having his majestic freedom stripped away, yet his rage must remain 'quiet' and suppressed because he is entirely powerless against the concrete walls and iron bars of his cage.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Literary device: Oxymoron (quiet + rage)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Meaning: Suppressed, impotent fury due to helplessness behind iron bars</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p3_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p3_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does the tiger do at night in the zoo? What do his brilliant eyes look at?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>At night, when human visitors depart, the tiger listens to the distant, mechanical sounds of the patrolling guard cars. He stares longing into the night sky with his brilliant, luminous eyes at the brilliant, sparkling stars, silently yearning for the boundless freedom of the cosmic universe.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Listens to the last mechanical sounds of patrolling guard cars</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Stares with brilliant eyes at brilliant stars, yearning for lost freedom</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p3_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p3_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does 'A Tiger in the Zoo' present a powerful ethical critique of human entertainment at the cost of animal subjugation?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Deprivation of Sovereign Dignity:</strong><br>Leslie Norris strips away the romantic glamour of zoos to expose the cruel tragedy of wildlife incarceration. The tiger, nature's apex predator and lord of the forest, is reduced to a pathetic museum artifact for the casual entertainment of uncaring tourists.</p><p><strong>2. Emotional and Psychological Torment:</strong><br>The poem underscores the psychological devastation of captivity: pacing repetitive small steps, suppressing primal hunting instincts, and enduring mechanical noises instead of nocturnal forest sounds.</p><p><strong>3. Poetic Juxtaposition:</strong><br>The repetition of 'brilliant'—his brilliant eyes gazing at the brilliant stars—creates a poignant climax. Both eyes and stars share cosmic magnificence, yet the stars are eternally free in the boundless sky while the tiger remains chained in an artificial cage, pleading for animal rights.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ethical critique: Lord of the jungle reduced to a commodified exhibit</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Psychological trauma: Repetitive pacing, suppressed predatory instinct</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Symbolism of 'brilliant eyes' vs 'brilliant stars' representing lost freedom</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 12</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Competency-Based Evaluation</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Why does the tiger ignore the visitors who come to see him at the zoo?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The tiger ignores visitors because he holds them in silent, aristocratic contempt. He recognizes that they are merely curious voyeurs who gawk at his confinement without offering empathy or freedom. Aware of his current impotence behind iron bars, he refuses to acknowledge them, maintaining his quiet pride by turning his back on their gaze.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(11)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(13)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","13":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch13\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">13</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 4: How to Tell Wild Animals</h2>\n      <p>Carolyn Wells — Humor, Parody & Linguistic Wordplay — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">If ever you should go by chance\nTo jungles in the east;\nAnd if there should to you advance\nA large and tawny beast,\nIf he roars at you as you’re dyin’\nYou’ll know it is the Asian Lion...\n\nOr if some time when roaming round,\nA noble wild beast greets you,\nWith black stripes on a yellow ground,\nJust notice if he eats you.\nThis simple rule may help you learn\nThe Bengal Tiger to discern.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Carolyn Wells</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p4_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p4_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does the poet distinguish between the Asian Lion and the Bengal Tiger?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Asian Lion:</strong> The Asian Lion is found in the eastern jungles; it is a large and tawny-colored beast that terrifies you with a mighty roar so deafening that you feel you are dying of fear.</p><p><strong>2. Bengal Tiger:</strong> The Bengal Tiger is a 'noble wild beast' with distinct black stripes on a yellow ground. The humorous identification rule is that you will know it is a tiger only when it pounces upon and eats you!</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Asian Lion: Large, tawny coat, roars ferociously while you're dying</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Bengal Tiger: Noble beast, black stripes on yellow coat; 'notice if he eats you'</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p4_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p4_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What humorous characteristics does the poet provide for the Leopard, the Bear, and the Hyena/Crocodile?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Leopard:</strong> Has a peppered, spotted hide; it will leap and leap upon you (<em>'lep and lep again'</em>), and roaring with pain will do no good.</p><p><strong>2. Bear:</strong> Found in your yard, it will greet you with a ferocious 'bear hug' that crushes the life out of you.</p><p><strong>3. Hyena vs Crocodile:</strong> Hyenas always appear with merry, deceptive smiles, while weeping tears belong to the deadly crocodile swallows its prey.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Leopard: Peppered spots, leaping repeatedly despite your screams</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Bear: Crushing lethal 'hug'</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Hyena smiles vs weeping Crocodile tears</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p4_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p4_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Carolyn Wells describe the chameleon, and how is it different from a lizard?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>A true chameleon is a small reptile shaped like a lizard, but unlike a lizard, it has no ears and not a single wing. If you look at a tree and see nothing at all, that is the chameleon camouflaging its skin to match the tree bark.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Traits: Small lizard-like reptile with no ears and no wings</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Camouflage: Invisible on tree bark because it changes color</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p4_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p4_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Analyze the comic techniques, poetic license, and irony in 'How to Tell Wild Animals'.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Parody of Educational Wildlife Guides:</strong><br>Carolyn Wells parodies conventional zoological handbooks by providing absurd identification tests where the confirmation of the animal's identity occurs only after the observer has been devoured or mauled to death.</p><p><strong>2. Poetic License & Linguistic Puns:</strong><br>The poet deliberately invents and bends English spelling and syntax to maintain comic rhyme: writing <em>'dyin''</em> to rhyme with <em>'lion'</em>, and creating <em>'lep and lep again'</em> instead of 'leap' to achieve dynamic, snappy rhyming.</p><p><strong>3. Incongruity and Irony:</strong><br>Calling a man-eating tiger 'noble' and a bone-crushing bear's attack an affectionate 'hug' subverts fear into comic delight through dramatic understatement.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Parody: Fatal confirmation rules (learning identity only after being eaten)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Poetic license: Invented spellings ('dyin'', 'lep') to fit rhyme scheme</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Understatement and irony: 'Noble' predator, deadly bear 'hug'</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 13</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Poetic Devices & Language</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Explain the rhyme scheme and meter used in the poem. How does it enhance the humorous tone?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The poem uses a regular six-line stanza structure with the rhyme scheme **ababcc**. The rhythmic, jaunty iambic meter gives the verses a nursery-rhyme sing-song lightness. By pairing lighthearted rhyming couplets with lethal jungle predators, the meter creates comic incongruity, rendering terrifying beasts thoroughly amusing.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(12)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(14)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","14":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch14\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">14</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 5: The Ball Poem</h2>\n      <p>John Berryman — Epistemology of Loss, Maturity & Material Transience — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">What is the boy now, who has lost his ball,\nWhat, what is he to do? I saw it go\nMerrily bouncing, down the street, and then\nMerrily over — there it is in the water!\nNo use to say ‘O there are other balls’:\nAn ultimate shaking grief fixes the boy\nAs he stands rigid, trembling, staring down\nAll his young days into the harbour where\nHis ball went. I would not intrude on him;\nA dime, another ball, is worthless. Now\nHe senses first responsibility\nIn a world of possessions. People will take\nBalls, balls will be lost always, little boy.\nAnd no one buys a ball back. Money is external.\nHe is learning, well behind his desperate eyes,\nThe epistemology of loss, how to stand up\nKnowing what every man must one day know\nAnd most know many days, how to stand up.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— John Berryman</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p5_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p5_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why does the poet say: 'I would not intrude on him; a dime, another ball, is worthless'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The poet refuses to intervene or buy the boy a replacement ball because the lost ball is irreplaceable in its emotional value. The ball was not merely a ten-cent rubber toy; it was steeped in personal memories of the boy's childhood years. Offering him money or another ball would trivialized his genuine grief and rob him of an essential rite of passage—learning how to confront personal loss independently.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Emotional value: Ball symbolized memories of his young childhood days</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Pedagogical restraint: Intervening with money robs him of learning resilience</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p5_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p5_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does the poet mean by 'in a world of possessions'? What is 'first responsibility'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>A 'world of possessions' refers to a materialistic society where people covet, accumulate, and identify with physical property. In such a world, the boy senses his 'first responsibility'—the sober realization that one must protect what one cherishes, and that material things can be permanently lost or destroyed without replacement.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">World of possessions: Materialistic society focused on ownership</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">First responsibility: Owning consequences and accepting transience</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p5_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p5_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does 'epistemology of loss' mean in the poem?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>'Epistemology' is the philosophical study of the nature of knowledge. The 'epistemology of loss' means understanding the fundamental reality, nature, and truth of loss—learning what it truly feels like to lose something precious, and acquiring the mental strength to survive grief and stand up again.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Definition: Understanding the philosophical nature and truth of loss</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Application: Developing emotional resilience to stand up after heartbreak</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p5_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p5_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">'Money is external. And no one buys a ball back.' How does John Berryman elevate the loss of a simple ball to a universal meditation on the human condition?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Symbolism of the Ball:</strong><br>The bouncing ball is a poignant metaphor for childhood innocence, pure joy, and loved ones. When the ball rolls into the dark harbor water, the boy sees <em>'all his young days'</em> swallowed up by the abyss, marking the end of carefree innocence.</p><p><strong>2. Limitations of Material Wealth:</strong><br>By asserting that <em>'Money is external'</em>, Berryman emphasizes that currency can only purchase physical, commodified substitutes. Money cannot repurchase lost time, departed loved ones, shattered relationships, or lost innocence. <em>'No one buys a ball back'</em> means that certain life experiences are absolute and irreversible.</p><p><strong>3. Universal Human Maturity:</strong><br>Every human being must inevitably face bereavement, disillusionment, and loss. True adulthood begins when one learns to stand upright in the wake of tragedy, accepting loss not as an anomaly, but as the foundational law of human existence.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ball as metaphor for childhood innocence and irreplaceable attachments</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Critique of wealth: Money is external and cannot buy back lost moments</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Universal philosophy: Maturing by learning 'how to stand up' after loss</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 14</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Psychological Insight</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does Berryman's stance of non-interference align with modern emotional counseling for children experiencing disappointment?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Modern developmental psychology stresses that overprotecting children from grief or instantly replacing lost belongings fosters emotional fragility and entitlement. By letting the child stand rigid, tremble, and process his own grief, the poet respects the boy's psychological dignity. Experiencing and processing sadness naturally builds coping mechanisms, enabling the child to develop authentic emotional resilience.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(13)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(15)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","15":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch15\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">15</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 6: Amanda!</h2>\n      <p>Robin Klein — Adolescent Autonomy, Parental Nagging & Escapist Reverie — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">Don’t bite your nails, Amanda!\nDon’t hunch your shoulders, Amanda!\nStop that slouching and sit up straight,\nAmanda!\n\n(There is a languid, emerald sea,\nwhere the sole inhabitant is me—\na mermaid, drifting blissfully.)\n\nDid you finish your homework, Amanda?\nDid you tidy your room, Amanda?\nI thought I told you to clean your shoes,\nAmanda!\n\n(I am an orphan, roaming the street.\nI pattern soft dust with my hushed, bare feet.\nThe silence is golden, the freedom is sweet.)</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Robin Klein</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p6_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p6_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How old do you think Amanda is? What nagging instructions are constantly hurled at her?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Amanda is a young adolescent schoolgirl, likely around ten to twelve years old, as indicated by her homework, acne breakouts, and untidy room. Her parent perpetually pesters her with negative behavioral commands: not to bite her nails, not to hunch her shoulders, to sit up straight, to finish her homework, to clean her room and shoes, not to eat chocolates, and not to sulk or look moody.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Age deduction: ~10–12 years (school homework, acne breakouts, room)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Commands: Posture, nail-biting, chores, shoes, chocolate restrictions</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p6_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p6_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why are stanzas 2, 4, and 6 placed in parentheses? Who speaks in them?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The parenthetical stanzas represent Amanda's internal mental reveries and subconscious escapism. While the odd stanzas represent the harsh, authoritative external voice of her nagging parent, the bracketed stanzas give voice to Amanda's silent soul retreating into fantasy worlds. The parentheses physically shelter her thoughts from the loud intrusions of the adult world.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Parentheses denote internal subconscious thoughts / daydreaming</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Contrast: External parent nagging vs Amanda's silent escapist sanctuary</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p6_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p6_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What three personas does Amanda fantasize about adopting? What does each fantasy reveal?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Mermaid:</strong> In a languid, emerald sea, drifting blissfully as the sole inhabitant, revealing her craving for peace, beauty, and solitude.</p><p><strong>2. Orphan:</strong> Roaming barefoot on silent streets making patterns in the dust, where <em>'silence is golden, freedom is sweet'</em>, revealing that she would rather be parentless than endure constant scolding.</p><p><strong>3. Rapunzel:</strong> Living in a high, secluded tower with tranquil, rare life, though she resolves never to let down her bright hair so that no rescuer can ever disturb her solitude.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mermaid: Solitary bliss in emerald sea</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Orphan: Sweet freedom and golden silence on dusty streets</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Rapunzel: Untouched tranquility in tower, refusing to drop hair</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p6_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p6_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does 'Amanda!' capture the universal tug-of-war between well-intentioned parental conditioning and an adolescent's yearning for space?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Smothering Parental Hovering:</strong><br>Amanda's parent is not abusive, but suffers from obsessive micro-management. In attempting to mold Amanda into an impeccable, disciplined lady fit for polite society, the parent bombards her with relentless criticism, destroying her self-esteem and natural joy.</p><p><strong>2. Defense Mechanism of Reverie:</strong><br>Unable to argue openly, Amanda builds psychological fortresses through imaginative withdrawal. Her daydream of being an orphan is particularly poignant and shocking—it demonstrates that excessive parental badgering can make a child feel that orphanhood is preferable to life under authoritarian surveillance.</p><p><strong>3. Final Irony:</strong><br>The poem ends with the parent reprimanding her: <em>'Stop that sulking at once, Amanda!... Anyone would think that I nagged at you, Amanda!'</em> The parent is completely blind to her own incessant nagging, worrying only about public perception.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Parental micro-management suffocating adolescent individuality</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Escapism & tragic wish for orphanhood as a defense against badgering</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Final irony: Parent accusing child of sulking while denying own nagging</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 15</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Parent-Child Communication</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How can parents balance instilling good manners and hygiene without driving their children into complete emotional detachment like Amanda?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Effective parenting requires empathy, active listening, and respecting personal boundaries rather than issuing endless negative imperatives ('Don't do this, don't do that'). If behavioral guidance is offered through dialogue, positive reinforcement, and collaborative discussions rather than public scolding and micro-management, children feel valued rather than smothered, eliminating the psychological urge to escape into isolated fantasies.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(14)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(16)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","16":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch16\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">16</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 7: The Trees</h2>\n      <p>Adrienne Rich — Ecological Liberation, Eco-Feminism & Subversion of Domesticity — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">The trees inside are moving out into the forest,\nthe forest that was empty all these days\nwhere no bird could sit\nno insect hide\nno sun bury its feet in shadow\nthe forest that was empty all these nights\nwill be full of trees by morning.\n\nAll night the roots work\nto disengage themselves from the cracks\nin the veranda floor.\nThe leaves strain toward the glass\nsmall twigs stiff with exertion\nlong-cramped boughs shuffling under the roof\nlike newly discharged patients\nhalf-dazed, moving\nto the clinic doors.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Adrienne Rich</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p7_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p7_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Where are the trees in the poem? Why is the forest empty? What will happen by morning?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The trees are unnaturally imprisoned inside the domestic space of human houses—in verandas and living rooms as decorative houseplants. The natural forest outside has been completely empty because human deforestation and commercial exploitation stripped it bare, leaving no trees for birds to perch, insects to hide, or sunlight to cast shadows. By morning, the rebellious trees will break free from human houses and repopulate the forest.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Trees currently trapped inside houses as indoor decorative plants</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Empty forest: Devoid of birds, insects, and shadows due to human deforestation</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Resolution: Trees breaking out all night to repopulate the forest by dawn</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p7_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p7_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What physical struggle do the roots, leaves, twigs, and boughs undergo to break free?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The trees wage a fierce, silent midnight rebellion:</p><ul><li><strong>Roots:</strong> Work tirelessly all night to disengage themselves from cracks in the veranda floor.</li><li><strong>Leaves:</strong> Strain urgently towards the window glass seeking light and freedom.</li><li><strong>Twigs:</strong> Grow stiff and taut with desperate exertion.</li><li><strong>Boughs:</strong> Shuffled under the roof like half-dazed, newly discharged hospital patients stumbling toward clinic doors.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Roots disengaging from veranda floor cracks</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Leaves and twigs straining against window glass</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Boughs compared to newly discharged, dazed hospital patients</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p7_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p7_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What happens to the house and the moon when the trees break into the open night?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The glass panes shatter as the trees march triumphantly outside into the fresh night winds. The sky opens up, and the moon, which appeared whole in the unobstructed sky, now looks broken into fractured pieces like a shattered mirror, crowned in the canopy of the tallest oak tree.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Window glass shatters; night winds rush out to greet trees</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Moon appears fractured like a broken mirror in the branches of the tall oak</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p7_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p7_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Adrienne Rich use 'The Trees' as a double allegory for both ecological reclamation and feminist emancipation?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Ecological Dimension:</strong><br>On a literal level, the poem portrays the unnatural imprisonment of nature by humans who reduce living wilderness to decorative indoor pots while razing natural forests. Nature reclaims its sovereign majesty by breaking domestic glass and returning to the wild.</p><p><strong>2. Eco-Feminist Allegory:</strong><br>As a passionate feminist poet, Adrienne Rich uses 'trees' as an extended metaphor for women who have historically been confined to domestic interiors—verandas, kitchens, and living rooms—repressed by patriarchal norms. The roots uncoupling from the floor represent women shattering societal shackles. The fractured moon crowned in the oak symbolizes female empowerment, reclaiming their rightful space in the public arena.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Literal / ecological level: Nature rebelling against domestic captivity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Feminist allegory: Women breaking out of domestic confinement into the world</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Symbolism of shattered glass and oak crown representing victory</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 16</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Poetic Simile & Personification</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Why does the poet compare the boughs to 'newly discharged patients'? Explain the psychological aptness of this simile.</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Newly discharged hospital patients are weak, unsteady on their feet, dazed by bright sunlight after long confinement, yet ecstatic to leave medical captivity. Similarly, the tree branches have been bent and stunted under the low domestic ceilings of human houses. As they emerge into open air, they are half-dazed and disoriented by sudden vastness, yet driven by an unstoppable urge to regain natural health in the forest.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(15)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(17)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","17":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch17\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">17</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 8: Fog</h2>\n      <p>Carl Sandburg — Extended Metaphor, Urban Vignette & Haiku-like Minimalism — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">The fog comes\non little cat feet.\n\nIt sits looking\nover harbour and city\non silent haunches\nand then moves on.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Carl Sandburg</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p8_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p8_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does Sandburg compare the fog to? Mention three points of similarity between the fog and a cat.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Carl Sandburg compares the fog to a <strong>cat</strong>. The three striking points of similarity are:</p><ol><li><strong>Silent Arrival:</strong> Just as a cat prowls stealthily without making a sound on soft padded paws, the fog rolls in quietly over the city unnoticed.</li><li><strong>Silent Sitting & Watching:</strong> Just as a cat sits curled up on its haunches calmly observing its surroundings, the fog settles over the harbor and city, silently overlooking everything.</li><li><strong>Mysterious Departure:</strong> Just as a cat quietly gets up and vanishes without warning, the fog lifts and dissipates silently.</li></ol>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Comparison identified: Fog compared to a cat</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Three parallels: Silent arrival on little feet, sitting on haunches, quiet departure</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p8_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p8_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What is the significance of the phrase 'on silent haunches'?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>'Haunches' refers to the hips or thighs of an animal. When a cat sits on its haunches with knees bent, it is motionless, alert, and ready to spring at any second. Similarly, the fog temporarily blankets the harbor and city in complete stillness, pausing briefly before evaporating into the atmosphere.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Literal posture: Sitting on folded hind legs in calm alertness</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Poetic resonance: Capturing the temporary, poised stillness of the blanketed fog</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p8_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p8_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">In just six lines and twenty-one words, Carl Sandburg creates an immortal impressionist masterpiece. Analyze the poetic minimalism of 'Fog'.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Extended Metaphor (Conceit):</strong><br>The entire poem is built upon a single unbroken metaphor without using 'like' or 'as'. Instead of writing an elaborate description of meteorological moisture, Sandburg personifies the fog as a living, feline creature.</p><p><strong>2. Haiku Influence and Free Verse:</strong><br>Influenced by Japanese Haiku and Imagism, the poem has no strict meter or end-rhyme. The brevity forces the reader to visualize the image intensely: the soft footfalls, the blanketed skyline, the quiet crouch over the docks, and the sudden vanishing.</p><p><strong>3. Contrast between Nature and Urban Industrialism:</strong><br>By enveloping a bustling industrial landscape ('harbour and city' with ships, cranes, and skyscrapers) in the soft, mysterious stillness of a cat, Sandburg demonstrates how nature effortlessly softens human machinery.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Extended metaphor without similes (pure metaphor / personification)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Influence of imagism and haiku brevity (zero wasted syllables)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Contrast between quiet natural element and noisy urban industrial city</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 17</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Extract & Style Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Does the poem contain any rhyme scheme? How does the free-verse form contribute to the poem's atmosphere?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>No, the poem is composed in free verse with no set rhyme or uniform meter. The unrhymed, irregular lines flow naturally like drifting mist. The absence of rigid rhyme matches the shapeless, fluid, unpredictable movement of fog creeping over the city.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(16)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(18)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","18":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch18\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">18</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 9: The Tale of Custard the Dragon</h2>\n      <p>Ogden Nash — Parody, Mock-Heroic Ballad & True Bravery vs Boasting — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">Belinda lived in a little white house,\nWith a little black kitten and a little grey mouse,\nAnd a little yellow dog and a little red wagon,\nAnd a realio, trulio, little pet dragon.\n\nNow the name of the little black kitten was Ink,\nAnd the little grey mouse, she called him Blink,\nAnd the little yellow dog was sharp as Mustard,\nBut the dragon was a coward, and she called him Custard.\n\nCustard the dragon had big sharp teeth,\nAnd spikes on top of him and scales underneath,\nMouth like a fireplace, chimney for a nose,\nAnd realio, trulio daggers on his toes.</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— Ogden Nash</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p9_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p9_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who lived with Belinda in her little white house? What were their names and descriptions?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Belinda lived with four companion pets:</p><ul><li><strong>Ink:</strong> A little black kitten as bold as a lion who chased lions down the stairs.</li><li><strong>Blink:</strong> A little grey mouse who lived in a mouse-hole.</li><li><strong>Mustard:</strong> A fierce little yellow dog as brave as a tiger in a rage.</li><li><strong>Custard:</strong> A cowardly pet dragon with sharp teeth, spikes on top, scales underneath, and a fireplace mouth, who always wept for a nice safe cage.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ink (black kitten) and Blink (grey mouse) enumerated</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mustard (brave yellow dog) described</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Custard (cowardly dragon wanting a safe cage) described</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p9_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p9_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Belinda and her pets boast of their courage and tease Custard?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Belinda claimed to be as brave as a barrel full of bears; Ink and Blink chased lions down the stairs; Mustard was as brave as an enraged tiger. They ruthlessly mocked Custard for his lack of courage, tickling him unmercifully and comparing him to 'Percival' (King Arthur's knight mocked for cowardice), laughing until the house shook.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Boasts: Belinda (barrel of bears), Ink/Blink (chasing lions), Mustard (tiger)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Teasing: Tickled unmercifully, called him 'Percival' in mock court</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p9_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p9_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Describe the appearance of the pirate who climbed into Belinda's house.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The intruder was a fearsome pirate climbing in through the window with a pistol in his left hand, a pistol in his right hand, and a gleaming cutlass held between his teeth. He had a sinister black beard and one wooden peg leg, making it abundantly clear that he meant serious harm.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Weapons: Pistol in each hand and bright cutlass in his teeth</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Appearance: Black beard, wooden leg, hostile criminal intent</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p9_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p9_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did each pet react when the pirate attacked? How did Custard save them?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Cowardice of the Boasters:</strong> Belinda paled and cried for help; Mustard yelped in terror and fled; Ink slinked down to the bottom of the household; Blink strategically hid in his mouse-hole.</p><p><strong>2. Custard's Heroic Attack:</strong> Custard leaped up snorting like an engine, clashing his tail like irons in a dungeon. He attacked the pirate like a robin at a worm, swallow-gulping the pirate whole after the pirate fired two useless bullets.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fleeing boasters: Belinda screamed, Mustard fled, Ink and Blink hid</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Custard's heroics: Snorting, clashing tail, devouring the pirate whole</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p9_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p9_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How is 'The Tale of Custard the Dragon' a mock-heroic ballad that reveals the difference between empty boasting and authentic courage?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Mock-Heroic Ballad Parody:</strong><br>A ballad traditionally narrates heroic deeds in solemn verse. Ogden Nash parodies this genre by featuring whimsical pets, comic rhyming words (<em>'realio, trulio'</em>), and an inversion of roles: the fierce dragon is a gentle pacifist while the mouse and kitten claim lion-taming courage.</p><p><strong>2. Authentic Courage vs Vain Boasting:</strong><br>When real existential danger strikes, all the loud braggarts flee in panic. The supposedly 'cowardly' Custard instantly risks his life to protect his family without boasting. After the crisis passes, the other pets resume making excuses (Mustard saying he would have been twice as brave if not flustered), and gentle Custard humbly agrees that everyone is braver than him, demonstrating true nobility.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Parody of heroic ballad form with whimsical rhymes ('realio, trulio')</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Contrast between crisis action (Custard) vs panic (Ink, Blink, Mustard)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Post-crisis humility: Boasters making excuses while Custard remains modest</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 18</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Value-Based Reflection</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> What moral does the poem teach about judging people based on self-promotion versus concrete actions?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The poem illustrates that those who brag the loudest about their bravery and accomplishments are usually the first to collapse when real adversity arrives. True courage is quiet, unassuming, and reveals itself through deeds rather than empty rhetoric. Custard's genuine heroism paired with modesty teaches that humility and readiness to act define real strength.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(17)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(19)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","19":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch19\" data-book=\"First Flight Poetry\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">19</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FIRST FLIGHT POETRY</div>\n      <h2>Poem 10: For Anne Gregory</h2>\n      <p>William Butler Yeats — Outer Glamour vs Inner Soul & Unconditional Divine Love — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"poem-display-box\">\n    <div class=\"poem-body\">“Never shall a young man, thrown\nInto despair\nBy those great honey-coloured\nRamparts at your ear,\nLove you for yourself alone\nAnd not your yellow hair.”\n\n“But I can get a hair-dye\nAnd set such colour there,\nBrown, or black, or carrot,\nThat young men in despair\nMay love me for myself alone\nAnd not my yellow hair.”\n\n“I heard an old religious man\nBut yesternight declare\nThat he had found a text to prove\nThat only God, my dear,\nCould love you for yourself alone\nAnd not your yellow hair.”</div>\n    <div class=\"poet-name\">— William Butler Yeats</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p10_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p10_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does the speaker mean by 'those great honey-coloured ramparts at your ear'? What effect do they have on young men?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>'Ramparts' are high defensive walls surrounding a fort or castle. Here, Yeats uses 'ramparts' as a striking metaphor for Anne Gregory's voluminous, glowing golden-yellow hair falling over her ears. Just as a fortress wall keeps intruders out, her stunning hair acts as a barrier that dazzles young men, throwing them into romantic despair and blinding them to her true internal personality.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Metaphor explained: Voluminous yellow hair compared to defensive castle walls</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Effect: Dazzles suitors into romantic despair, blinding them to inner self</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p10_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p10_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does the young woman (Anne Gregory) propose to do to test her suitors' love?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Anne Gregory responds that she can easily alter her outward appearance by dyeing her hair brown, black, or carrot-colored. By shedding her prized golden locks, she hopes to repel superficial suitors and attract someone who will love her for her inner character, intellect, and soul rather than her external beauty.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Action: Dyeing hair brown, black, or carrot-colored</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Objective: Testing suitors so they love her for herself alone, not hair</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p10_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p10_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What did the old religious man declare he had found in a sacred text?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The speaker reveals that just the previous night, an old religious man had quoted an ancient sacred text proving that only God has the divine capacity to love a human being for themselves alone, looking past their physical attributes. Mortals are inherently flawed and inevitably swayed by outward physical appearance.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Declaration: Found sacred scriptural text proving divine love</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Core truth: Only God loves inner soul unconditionally; mortals are swayed by looks</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"p10_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('p10_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Critically evaluate W.B. Yeats' dialogue on the tension between superficial physical attraction and spiritual love in 'For Anne Gregory'.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Superficiality of Human Love:</strong><br>Yeats addresses the universal human longing to be appreciated for one's intrinsic personality, intellect, and moral worth rather than physical skin and hair. However, he candidly points out that human attraction is inescapably visual and sensory; young men are captivated by external physical beauty ('honey-coloured ramparts').</p><p><strong>2. Anne's Naive Idealism:</strong><br>Anne Gregory naively believes that by simply dyeing her hair a less glamorous color, she can filter out shallow suitors. She fails to see that humans will merely switch to admiring other physical traits.</p><p><strong>3. The Sublimity of Divine Love:</strong><br>The poem concludes on a profound spiritual note: unconditional love that transcends physical form is a divine virtue possessed solely by the Creator. To expect flawed mortals to love purely without physical aesthetic attraction is to demand divine perfection from human nature.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Human aesthetic attraction vs desire for inner spiritual appreciation</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Critique of Anne's idea that altering hair color solves superficiality</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Theological conclusion: Only God possesses truly unconditional love</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 19</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Philosophical & Cultural Reflection</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> In the era of social media filters and cosmetic surgery, how does 'For Anne Gregory' critique modern obsession with physical appearances?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Yeats' century-old poem anticipated modern society's intense anxiety over physical packaging. Digital media and cosmetic trends commodify looks just like Anne's 'yellow hair', confusing external photogenic beauty with personal worth. The poem reminds us that while physical beauty is transient, superficial, and easily manufactured (through hair-dye or filters), true selfhood resides in the eternal spirit within.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(18)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(20)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","20":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch20\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">20</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 1: A Triumph of Surgery</h2>\n      <p>James Herriot — Pampered Affection vs Sensible Care — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp1_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp1_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why is Mrs Pumphrey worried about Tricki? What symptoms does Tricki exhibit?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Mrs Pumphrey is frantic with worry because her pampered little dog Tricki has become listless, bloated, and utterly inactive. He looks like a bloated sausage with a leg at each corner; his eyes are bloodshot and rheumy, his tongue lolls from his jaws, and he refuses to eat even his favorite delicacies, having frequent bouts of vomiting while lying down panting on a rug.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Physical appearance: Bloated sausage, bloodshot and rheumy eyes</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Behavioral symptoms: Complete listlessness, refusing food, vomiting, panting</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp1_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp1_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What mistakes did Mrs Pumphrey make in feeding Tricki? Did she follow Dr. Herriot's advice?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Assuming Tricki was suffering from malnutrition, Mrs Pumphrey overindulged him by feeding him extra malt, cod-liver oil, and bowls of Horlicks between meals, along with cream cakes and chocolates. She completely ignored Dr. Herriot's strict warnings to cut down on sweets, give him regular exercise, and keep him on a strict diet, thereby causing his severe illness through excessive pampering.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Overfeeding: Malt, cod-liver oil, Horlicks, cream cakes, chocolates</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Failure to follow doctor's advice on strict diet and exercise</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp1_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp1_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Dr. Herriot treat Tricki at his surgery? Did he administer any medicine or surgery?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Dr. Herriot administered zero medication and performed no surgery whatsoever. His treatment consisted of a strictly sensible natural regimen:</p><ul><li>For the first two days, Tricki was given no food at all, only plenty of fresh water.</li><li>On the third day, Tricki showed interest in his surroundings and whined at the door.</li><li>He was introduced into the pack of surgery dogs where he jostled for food, ran across the yard, and wrestled, rapidly shedding fat and regaining muscular health.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Zero medicines and zero surgery administered</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fasting on water for two days to detoxify digestive system</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Vigorous natural exercise playing with other dogs in the pack</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp1_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp1_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why was Dr. Herriot tempted to keep Tricki on as a permanent guest at the surgery?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Dr. Herriot and his staff were tempted to retain Tricki because Mrs Pumphrey sent lavish supplies of fresh eggs (two dozen at a time), bottles of fine wine to enrich Tricki's blood, and bottles of brandy. The doctor and his assistants enjoyed royal breakfasts with eggs, leisurely lunches with wine, and luxurious evenings by the fire with brandy, all at Mrs Pumphrey's expense!</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mrs Pumphrey sent lavish food items: 2 dozen fresh eggs, wine, and brandy</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Doctor and staff enjoyed luxurious meals every day</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp1_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp1_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why does Mrs Pumphrey proclaim Tricki's recovery as 'a triumph of surgery'? Contrast Mrs Pumphrey's suffocating indulgence with Dr. Herriot's pragmatic common sense.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Mrs Pumphrey's Exclamation:</strong><br>When Mrs Pumphrey arrives to collect Tricki after a fortnight, she is astonished to see him transformed into a lithe, hard-muscled, energetic animal who leaps into her lap licking her face. Overcome with emotional tears, she proclaims: <em>'Oh, Mr Herriot, how can I ever thank you? This is a triumph of surgery!'</em> In her aristocratic innocence, she assumes an extraordinary surgical marvel cured him.</p><p><strong>2. Contrast in Attitudes:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mrs Pumphrey (Blind Affection):</strong> Represents toxic overindulgence where love is equated with material luxury and overfeeding. Her inability to discipline Tricki nearly killed him through obesity and lethargy.</li><li><strong>Dr. Herriot (Pragmatic Professionalism):</strong> Represents medical integrity, common sense, and psychological insight. He recognized that Tricki's only ailment was overfeeding and lack of exercise. By enforcing natural fasting and socialization rather than prescribing unnecessary drugs, he cured the dog painlessly.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mrs Pumphrey's reaction: Believed a miraculous surgical intervention cured him</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Characterization of Mrs Pumphrey: Smothering love causing physical harm</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Characterization of Dr. Herriot: Professional pragmatism, common sense medicine</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 20</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Value-Based Application</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How is 'A Triumph of Surgery' a timeless warning to parents who overindulge their children with junk food and luxury without physical activity?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The story is an allegory for modern parental overindulgence. Wealthy parents often shower children with excessive fast food, gadgets, and sedentary luxury under the mistaken belief of providing affection. Like Tricki, children subjected to undisciplined pampering develop health complications and lethargy. True love involves setting healthy boundaries, teaching moderation, and ensuring physical activity rather than gratifying every fleeting desire.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(19)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(21)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","21":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch21\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">21</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 2: The Thief's Story</h2>\n      <p>Ruskin Bond — Redemption, Trust & The Transforming Power of Literacy — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp2_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp2_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who is the narrator (Hari Singh)? How does he win Anil's trust and enter his home?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Hari Singh is a seasoned fifteen-year-old thief and confidence trickster who changes his name every month to evade the police and his previous employers. He approaches twenty-five-year-old Anil at a wrestling match, flattering him with easy compliments. When Anil admits he has no money to hire him, Hari lies that he knows how to cook. Though his first meal is so atrocious that Anil gives it to stray dogs, Hari's disarming, appealing smile wins Anil over, and Anil agrees to teach him.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Identity: 15-year-old thief who changes names to escape police</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Strategy: Flattery, lying about cooking, and disarming smile to win trust</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp2_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp2_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What does Anil do for a living? How does he treat Hari Singh?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Anil is a struggling freelance writer who earns by fits and starts, writing articles for magazines. When he gets a cheque, he celebrates lavishly with friends, and when broke, he borrows and worries until the next payment. He treats Hari with exceptional kindness and patience: he teaches him to cook, write his name, write complete sentences, and add numbers, trusting him with the door key and grocery purchases.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Profession: Freelance writer for magazines; irregular income ('fits and starts')</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Treatment of Hari: Taught him reading, writing, math; granted keys and total trust</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp2_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp2_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does Hari Singh steal Anil's money? Why did he miss the 10:30 Express to Lucknow?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. The Theft:</strong> Anil brought home a bundle of six hundred rupees in fifty-rupee notes from selling a book to a publisher and tucked it under his mattress. At midnight, Hari crept silently into the room, slid his hand under the mattress, and slipped the money out without waking Anil.</p><p><strong>2. Missing the Train:</strong> Hari reached the railway station just as the 10:30 Express to Lucknow was chugging out. He could easily have jumped into one of the carriages, but an unexplainable hesitation and a stirring conscience held him back on the platform until the train vanished into the night.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Theft: Slipped 600 rupees in 50-rupee notes from under mattress</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Missing train: Subconscious prick of conscience and hesitation held him back</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp2_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp2_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why does Hari Singh decide to return to Anil and put the stolen money back?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Sitting drenched in the rain in the maidan, Hari analyzed the reactions of different men upon being robbed: the greedy man shows fear, the rich man shows anger, and the poor man shows acceptance. But Anil, he knew, would show only a touch of sadness—not for the loss of money, but for the loss of trust. Furthermore, Hari realized that stealing might give him six hundred rupees to live like an oil-rich Arab for a week, but learning to read and write sentences would make him a truly respected, clever, and great man. Driven by this desire for education and self-respect, he crept back and slipped the damp notes under Anil's mattress.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Anil's sadness would be for betrayal of trust, not loss of cash</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Realization that literacy and education offer true greatness, not theft</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp2_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp2_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">'A thief can be reformed not by punishment or prison, but by unconditional trust, forgiveness, and education.' Elucidate with reference to Anil and Hari Singh.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Limitations of Punitive Law:</strong><br>Standard judicial punishment rarely reforms criminals; prison often hardens resentment and refines criminal methods. Hari Singh had spent years cheating masters and dodging police, entirely unbothered by laws or reprimands.</p><p><strong>2. Anil's Method of Reformation:</strong><br>Anil's silent benevolence worked where police batons had failed:</p><ul><li>He offered absolute trust, giving a street boy the key to his house.</li><li>He offered education—the supreme tool of social transformation. By teaching Hari to write sentences, Anil opened the door to legitimate professional dignity.</li><li>The ultimate test arrived the morning after the theft. When Anil handed Hari a damp fifty-rupee note, promising to pay him regularly and announcing: <em>'Today we'll start writing sentences'</em>, Hari realized Anil knew about the nocturnal robbery and the rain-soaked cash. Yet, Anil spoke not a single word of blame, nor did he report him to the police.</li></ul><p>Anil's silent forgiveness and steadfast commitment to Hari's education permanently conquered the criminal in Hari, proving that unconditional empathy is the most potent moral catalyst for human redemption.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Critique of punitive punishment vs transformative power of empathy</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Anil's gift of literacy as the gateway to genuine self-respect and dignity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Climax: Damp 50-rupee note, silent forgiveness that reformed the thief forever</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 21</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Character & Ethical Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Why did Anil decide not to hand Hari Singh over to the police even after discovering the wet notes?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Anil possessed profound human wisdom. He understood that handing Hari to the police would brand him as a habitual criminal and push him deeper into the underworld. Anil recognized that Hari had overcome his own thieving instinct and walked back through the rainy night solely out of loyalty and a yearning for education. Anil rewarded this moral triumph with silent grace, choosing to save a soul rather than penalize a lapse.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(20)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(22)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","22":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch22\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">22</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 3: The Midnight Visitor</h2>\n      <p>Robert Arthur — Wit, Presence of Mind & Subversion of Stereotypes — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp3_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp3_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How is Ausable different from conventional secret agents depicted in spy thrillers?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Ausable shatters every Hollywood stereotype of a dashing, glamorous secret agent. He is exceptionally fat, sloppy, and clumsy. He speaks French and German with difficulty and retains a heavy American accent brought from Boston twenty years ago. Instead of operating from exotic, high-tech mansions with mysterious femmes fatales, he occupies a gloomy, musty room on the sixth and top floor of a rundown French hotel.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Physical contrast: Exceptionally fat, sloppy, heavy American accent</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Setting contrast: Gloomy, cheap room on 6th floor of a rundown French hotel</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp3_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp3_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who is Fowler, and why did he feel disillusioned upon meeting Ausable?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">2 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Fowler is a young, romantic writer who had envisioned espionage as a world of mysterious figures in the night, pistol shots, and drugs in the wine. He felt profoundly let down and bored when he found Ausable to be a fat, mundane man spending an ordinary evening in a dim music hall discussing reports.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Identity: Young, romantic mystery writer seeking thrills</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Disillusionment: Ausable's ordinary, fat appearance and dull routine</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp3_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp3_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who was the midnight intruder inside Ausable's room, and what did he demand?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The intruder was <strong>Max</strong>, a slender, crafty rival secret agent with the face of a fox. Standing in the center of the room with an automatic pistol pointed directly at Ausable, he demanded the top-secret military report concerning new missiles that Ausable was scheduled to receive that night, boasting that it would be safer in his hands.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Identity: Rival secret agent Max, slender with fox-like cunning</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mission: Stealing confidential missile report at gunpoint</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp3_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp3_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Ausable fabricate the story of the nonexistent balcony to trap Max?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Without showing a trace of panic, Ausable coolly sat down in an armchair and complained bitterly with convincing irritation that this was the second time in a month that someone had entered his room through that 'nuisance of a balcony' belonging to the next apartment. His calm, detailed description convinced Max that a real balcony extended directly beneath his window sill.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Feigned irritation about management failing to block the balcony</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Psychological deception: Made Max believe a balcony existed under window</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp3_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp3_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">'Presence of mind and sharp intellect are far deadlier than a loaded gun.' How does Ausable outwit and eliminate Max without firing a single shot?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Psychological Composure Under Gunpoint:</strong><br>When confronted by an armed assassin, Ausable neither screamed nor pleaded. He assessed Max's psychological makeup—cunning yet jittery—and immediately seized narrative control of the room.</p><p><strong>2. The Double Deception:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Fabricating the Balcony:</strong> He planted the false idea of an external balcony beneath the sixth-floor window.</li><li><strong>Weaponizing the Knock:</strong> When a sudden knock sounded at the door, Max panicked and asked who it was. Ausable smiled calmly and claimed it was the police, whom he had requested for extra protection for the secret missile paper.</li></ul><p><strong>3. The Fatal Plunge:</strong><br>Terrified of the 'police', Max stepped backwards onto the window sill, threatening Ausable with his gun, and dropped blindly into what he believed was a balcony. In reality, there was no balcony; Max fell six floors to his death on the pavement below. The door opened to reveal Henry the waiter with a tray, drinks, and glasses—proving that Ausable's mind had orchestrated the entire fatal trap.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Cool psychological control under gunpoint without physical weapon</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Balcony fabrication + claiming waiter's knock was police</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Climax: Max jumping into the void from 6th floor; waiter enters with drinks</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 22</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Narrative Technique</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does Robert Arthur use dramatic irony and twist ending to construct a brilliant suspense narrative in 'The Midnight Visitor'?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Arthur sets up expectations through Fowler's romantic notions of espionage, only to immediately dismantle them with Ausable's mundane reality. Suspense peaks when Max holds them at gunpoint, but Arthur reverses power dynamics through Ausable's dialogue. The dramatic irony lies in the fact that neither Max nor Fowler realizes that the 'balcony' and 'police' are figments of Ausable's quick wit until Max plunges to his death and the harmless waiter walks in with drinks.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(21)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(23)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","23":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch23\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">23</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 4: A Question of Trust</h2>\n      <p>Victor Canning — Flawed Morality, Deception & The Fall of a Gentleman Thief — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp4_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp4_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What kind of a person was Horace Danby? Why was he considered good and respectable, yet not completely honest?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Horace Danby was a fifty-year-old bachelor who lived with a housekeeper and ran a successful lock-making business with two assistants. He was universally regarded as a good, peaceful, and respectable citizen. However, he was not completely honest because fifteen years ago he had served a prison sentence, and he meticulously burgled one safe every year to finance his expensive passion for collecting rare and valuable books.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Respectable exterior: 50-year-old bachelor, successful lock-maker</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Secret crime: Past prison record, burgled one safe every year for rare books</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp4_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp4_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Horace prepare for his burglary at Shotover Grange? What physical ailment troubled him?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Horace studied Shotover Grange for two weeks, analyzing its rooms, electrical wiring, paths, and garden. He learned that the family was in London and the two servants had gone to the cinema. He befriended the pet dog Sherry by calling its name affectionately. However, he was troubled by a severe attack of hay fever caused by the scent of flowers in the drawing room, which made him sneeze repeatedly.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Meticulous planning: Studied house, servants' schedule, wiring, dog Sherry</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Physical affliction: Hay fever triggered by flowers, causing sneezing fits</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp4_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp4_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who is the young lady in red who confronts Horace Danby? How does she trick him?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>A charming, graceful young woman dressed in red appears in the doorway, pretending to be the mistress of Shotover Grange. She speaks with calm authority, pats the dog Sherry familiar with her, and claims she returned unexpectedly to collect her jewels for a party. She offers to let Horace escape without calling the police on one condition: that he crack open the safe for her because she has forgotten the numbers.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Appearance: Poised young woman in red posing as lady of the house</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Trick: Asked him to open safe claiming she forgot combination for party</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp4_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp4_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What fatal mistake did Horace commit while opening the safe for the lady in red?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Eager to please the lady and escape arrest, Horace took off his gloves to light her cigarette with his gold lighter. Forgetting to put his gloves back on, he cracked open the safe with his bare hands. While he handed her the jewels and walked away free, his fingerprints were left smeared all over the safe, the room, and the furniture.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Fatal error: Removed gloves to light her cigarette and didn't put them back</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Result: Left clear fingerprints all over the opened safe and room</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp4_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp4_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why does Horace Danby get furious whenever anyone speaks of 'honor among thieves'? Analyze the irony in 'A Question of Trust'.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Arrest and Betrayal:</strong><br>Two days later, Horace was arrested by the police based on his fingerprints found on the looted safe. The actual owner of Shotover Grange—a sharp-tongued, sixty-year-old grey-haired woman—declared that Horace's story of the charming young lady was sheer nonsense. Horace realized that the young woman in red was herself a professional burglar who had effortlessly manipulated him into doing the dirty work for her.</p><p><strong>2. The Irony of 'Honor Among Thieves':</strong><br>The traditional criminal adage 'honor among thieves' dictates that criminals should respect and protect fellow thieves. Horace, an old-school gentleman thief, had naively trusted the woman. However, the modern, ruthless female thief possessed zero loyalty; she used him as a scapegoat, leaving him to rot in prison while she enjoyed the jewels. Now working as the prison librarian, Horace boils with rage at the phrase because he was comprehensively outwitted and ruined by one of his own kind.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Horace arrested via fingerprints; real owner is 60-year-old grey-haired lady</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Realization: Lady in red was a fellow thief who used him as a scapegoat</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Irony: Betrayed by a fellow thief, making 'honor among thieves' a bitter mockery</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 23</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Critical Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> Horace Danby was a meticulous planner who never stole more than what he needed for books. Why did his intelligence fail so miserably against the lady in red?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Horace's intelligence failed because he suffered from class-based gullibility and panic. When confronted by a woman who exuded the poise, voice, and commanding aura of high aristocracy, he immediately bowed to her perceived authority. His acute fear of returning to prison clouded his analytical faculties, making him overlook obvious red flags—such as why the mistress would need a thief to break her own safe rather than calling a locksmith. His desire to appease a pretty, high-born woman blinded him to forensic basics.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(22)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(24)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","24":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch24\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">24</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 5: Footprints without Feet</h2>\n      <p>H.G. Wells — Scientific Hubris, Lawlessness & The Tragic Misuse of Genius — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp5_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp5_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did the invisible man first become visible in London? What had he done before that?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. First Becoming Visible:</strong> Two young boys in London were astonished to see fresh, muddy footprints appearing out of nowhere on the stone steps of a house. Griffin had stepped in mud, and as he walked, his muddy feet imprinted clear tracks in the snow before drying out and vanishing.</p><p><strong>2. Prior Action:</strong> Before this, Griffin had set fire to his landlord's house in revenge because the landlord disliked him and had tried to evict him. To escape unseen without arrest, Griffin swallowed his experimental drugs, stripped off all his clothes, and became an invisible, homeless wanderer in the freezing winter.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Visible through muddy footprints appearing on steps and pavement</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Prior deed: Burned down landlord's house in revenge and swallowed invisibility drug</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp5_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp5_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What did Griffin do inside the large London department store? What happened the next morning?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>To escape the bitter January cold, Griffin slipped into a large London store before closing. Once inside, he broke open boxes and fitted himself out with warm clothes, an overcoat, and shoes. He fed himself with cold meat and coffee from the restaurant, stole sweets and wine from the grocery, and slept comfortably on a pile of quilts. The next morning, when the store assistants arrived, he panicked, ran, and was forced to strip off his newly acquired clothes one by one to become invisible again, escaping empty-handed into the freezing air.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Store raid: Stole warm clothes, food (meat, coffee, wine), slept on quilts</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Morning escape: Panicked upon discovery, stripped naked in the freezing cold to escape</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp5_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp5_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What bizarre burglaries and supernatural events took place in the village of Iping?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Griffin arrived at Mrs Hall's inn in Iping wrapped in bandages with dark spectacles, a false nose, and bushy whiskers. Soon, two strange events occurred:</p><ul><li><strong>Clergyman's Burglary:</strong> The clergyman and his wife heard chinking money in their study at dawn. Looking inside with a poker, they found the room completely empty, yet their housekeeping money had vanished from the desk.</li><li><strong>Haunted Furniture:</strong> When Mr. and Mrs. Hall inspected Griffin's empty room, the bedroom chair suddenly sprang to life, charged at Mrs Hall, and pushed them both out of the room, slamming and locking the door behind them.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Theft at clergyman's house: Money stolen from desk in an empty room</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Haunted furniture: Bedroom chair sprang to life and attacked Mrs Hall</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp5_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp5_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Describe the dramatic confrontation between Griffin, Mrs Hall, and Constable Jaffers.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When Mrs Hall demanded an explanation for his empty-room antics, Griffin lost his temper and shouted: <em>'You don't understand who or what I am? Very well—I'll show you!'</em> He threw off his whiskers, spectacles, nose, and bandages, revealing a headless body to the horrified crowd. When Constable Jaffers arrived with a warrant to arrest him, Jaffers bravely attempted to arrest a man without a head. Griffin stripped off his shirt, socks, and pants, delivering invisible, savage blows to Jaffers and the villagers until the constable was knocked unconscious.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Griffin removed bandages, glasses, nose, becoming a headless torso</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Constable Jaffers' brave attempt; Griffin stripped naked and knocked him out</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp5_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp5_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">'Griffin was a brilliant scientist, but a lawless, antisocial monster.' Discuss how H.G. Wells warns against scientific discovery divorced from human morality.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Extraordinary Scientific Genius:</strong><br>Griffin was undoubtedly a brilliant physiologist who synthesized a miraculous chemical compound capable of making the human body transparent as a sheet of glass while remaining solid to the touch. This was a monumental scientific triumph.</p><p><strong>2. Moral Degradation and Lawlessness:</strong><br>Instead of utilizing his discovery for the betterment of medical science or mankind, Griffin's antisocial hubris turned him into a petty criminal, arsonist, thief, and murderer:</p><ul><li>He burned his landlord's property in petty revenge.</li><li>He stole food, clothes, and theater props in London, viciously attacking a shopkeeper from behind.</li><li>In Iping, he terrorized an entire village, robbed a priest, assaulted women, and battered a police officer.</li></ul><p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> Wells demonstrates that intellect without conscience is monstrous; scientific power divorced from empathy and ethics leads inevitably to isolation, paranoia, and self-destruction.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Recognition of scientific brilliance: Formulating invisibility formula</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Detailed catalogue of crimes: Arson, theft, assaults, terrorizing Iping</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Wells' philosophical warning: Science without ethics leads to monstrous destruction</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 24</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Ethics & Science</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does the character of Constable Jaffers serve as a moral foil to Griffin?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Constable Jaffers represents unwavering duty, public service, and lawfulness. Even when confronted with the terrifying, unnatural spectacle of a headless man, Jaffers steadfastly maintains that if the magistrate issued an arrest warrant, the man must be arrested, head or no head. In contrast to Griffin's lawless egoism, Jaffers exhibits selfless bravery in defending his community.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(23)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(25)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","25":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch25\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">25</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 6: The Making of a Scientist</h2>\n      <p>Robert W. Peterson — Curiosity, Scientific Rigor & The Shaping of a Prodigy — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp6_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp6_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did the children's book 'The Travels of Monarch X' become a turning point in Richard Ebright's life?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>By second grade, Ebright had collected all twenty-five species of butterflies found around his hometown of Reading, Pennsylvania, and was growing bored. His mother bought him <em>'The Travels of Monarch X'</em> by Dr. Fredrick A. Urquhart of the University of Toronto. The book described the migration of monarch butterflies to Central America and invited readers to tag butterflies for research. This opened the boundless universe of global scientific research to young Ebright, permanently sparking his scientific career.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Context: Exhausted local species collection by second grade</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Book's impact: Dr. Urquhart's monarch migration study and invitation to tag butterflies</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp6_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp6_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What lesson did Ebright learn when he lost at his first County Science Fair in seventh grade?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>In seventh grade, Ebright entered the County Science Fair with slides of frog tissues shown under a microscope, but won nothing while others took home awards. He realized that science is not merely about displaying pretty slides; real science requires designing and executing genuine, controlled experiments to test hypotheses. This epiphany ignited his determination to conduct authentic experimental biology.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Entry: Frog tissue slides under microscope (mere visual display)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Lesson learned: Real science demands authentic, hypothesis-driven experimentation</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp6_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp6_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What breakthrough discovery did Ebright make regarding the twelve gold spots on a monarch pupa?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Everyone previously assumed that the twelve tiny gold spots on a monarch pupa were purely ornamental decorations. Ebright and a fellow student built an electronic device that proved the spots were not decorative at all; they secreted a vital juvenile hormone necessary for the pupa's full metamorphosis into an adult butterfly. This discovery won him first prize at the County Science Fair and a seat in the International Science Fair.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Prevailing myth: Gold spots were purely ornamental decorations</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Discovery: Produced a vital growth hormone essential for pupal metamorphosis</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp6_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp6_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Ebright formulate his revolutionary theory about how cells read their DNA?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>While examining X-ray photos of the chemical structure of the hormone during his junior year at Harvard, Ebright had an epiphany: the hormone's molecular structure answered a fundamental riddle of biology. He realized that the cell can literally 'read' the blueprint of its DNA. Along with his roommate James R. Wong, he worked all night drawing diagrams, constructing plastic molecular models, and wrote a paper explaining that DNA directs heredity and cellular function, publishing it in a prestigious national science journal.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">X-ray photos of hormone revealed how cells read the blueprint of DNA</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Constructed molecular models with James Wong and published breakthrough theory</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp6_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp6_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What are the three essential ingredients in the making of a true scientist? What role did Ebright's mother and teacher play in his success?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Three Ingredients of a Scientist:</strong><br>According to the author, the recipe for a true scientist requires: (i) a first-rate mind, (ii) boundless curiosity, and (iii) the will to win for the right reasons—not for vanity or trophies, but to discover truth and excel at one's craft.</p><p><strong>2. Role of Mentors:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>His Mother:</strong> Was his constant companion after his father's death. She encouraged his curiosity, took him on trips, bought him telescopes, microscopes, cameras, and the fateful book on Monarchs, keeping him intellectually engaged every evening.</li><li><strong>Mr. Richard A. Weiherer (Social Studies Teacher):</strong> Channeled Ebright's drive into public speaking and model United Nations debates, admiring Ebright's integrity—that he was competitive not for greed, but because he demanded the best from himself in every field.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Three ingredients: First-rate mind, curiosity, will to win for right reasons</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mother's foundational role: Companion, intellectual driver, equipment provider</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mr. Weiherer's mentorship: Debating skills, guiding competitive spirit with integrity</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 25</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Competency-Based Evaluation</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does Ebright's journey demonstrate that scientific genius is not a genetic accident, but a product of sustained discipline, multi-disciplinary interests, and resilience?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Ebright was not merely an isolated lab biologist; he was a straight-A student, an accomplished debater, an outdoor canoeist, and an expert photographer. His multidisciplinary skills fed into his scientific vision—his ability to debate sharpened his scientific logic, while his photography aided his cellular imaging. When his initial experiments failed, he did not surrender; he refined his methodology. Genius is the cultivation of curiosity through relentless hard work.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(24)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(26)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","26":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch26\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">26</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 7: The Necklace</h2>\n      <p>Guy de Maupassant — Vanity, Borrowed Glory & The Bitter Price of Pride — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp7_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp7_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why was Matilda Loisel perpetually unhappy and discontented with her life?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Born into a family of clerks with no dowry or social prospects, Matilda felt born for all the delicacies and luxuries of aristocratic life. Instead, she married an ordinary clerk in the Ministry of Public Instruction. She suffered incessantly from the shabby walls, worn chairs, and modest food of her home, tormented by vivid daydreams of silent antechambers hung with Oriental tapestries, bronze torchieres, exquisite banquets on gleaming silver, and whispered flirtations in aristocratic salons.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Discontented because she believed she was born for aristocratic luxury</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Tormented by modest apartment and daydreams of wealth and high society</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp7_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp7_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Matilda react to the invitation to the Minister's ball? How did her husband arrange her dress and jewelry?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Her Spiteful Reaction:</strong> Instead of being delighted, Matilda threw the invitation spitefully across the table, weeping that she had nothing appropriate to wear to such an elite gathering.</p><p><strong>2. Arrangement:</strong> Her devoted husband sacrificed 400 francs he had saved to purchase a hunting gun to buy her a gown. To satisfy her craving for jewelry, she visited her wealthy school friend, Madame Forestier, who lent her a dazzling diamond necklace in a black satin box.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Angry and weeping because she lacked formal gown and jewels</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Husband gave 400 francs (hunting savings); borrowed diamond necklace from friend</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp7_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp7_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How was Matilda's experience at the ball? When and how was the necklace lost?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. Triumph at Ball:</strong> Matilda was an absolute sensation—the prettiest woman in the ballroom, elegant, gracious, smiling, and intoxicated with delight. All the cabinet attaches and the Minister noticed her, dancing until 4 a.m.</p><p><strong>2. The Loss:</strong> Returning home, she rushed to the mirror to admire herself in her final glory and uttered a shriek of horror: the diamond necklace was missing from her neck. It had slipped off unnoticed either in the carriage or on the streets.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Ball triumph: Prettiest woman, intoxicated with admiration and joy</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Loss: Discovered missing before mirror at home; lost in carriage/street</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp7_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp7_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did the Loisels replace the lost necklace? What financial ruin did they plunge into?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Unable to find the necklace, they located an identical diamond necklace at the Palais-Royal priced at 36,000 francs. Loisel used his 18,000 francs inheritance from his father and borrowed the remaining 18,000 francs from usurers and loan sharks at ruinous interest rates. To repay this crushing debt, they dismissed their maid, rented a cheap garret, and spent ten brutal years in grinding poverty.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Replacement cost: 36,000 francs (used 18,000 inheritance + 18,000 usurious debt)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Consequences: Dismissed maid, moved to attic, 10 years of grueling labor</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp7_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp7_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did ten years of grueling poverty transform Matilda physically and emotionally?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The ten years of harsh physical labor aged Matilda terribly. She became the crude, loud, muscular woman of an impoverished working-class household, with untidy hair, red coarse hands, and skirt askew, washing greasy pots and scrubbing floors. Yet she bore her burden with heroic resignation, having paid off her debt with her own sweat and dignity.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Physical transformation: Aged, coarse red hands, loud voice, untidy skirts</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Moral shift: Hard working-class stoicism; paid debts with heroic labor</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp7_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp7_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What shocking truth does Madame Forestier reveal at the end of the story? What is the supreme irony of Matilda Loisel's life?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. The Shocking Climax:</strong><br>Meeting Madame Forestier on the Champs-Elysees ten years later, Matilda proudly reveals that her lost beauty was due to replacing the lost diamond necklace at a cost of 36,000 francs. Deeply touched, Madame Forestier clasps Matilda's worn hands and exclaims with pity: <em>'Oh! My poor Matilda! Mine were false. They were not worth over five hundred francs!'</em></p><p><strong>2. Supreme Irony of Fate:</strong><br>The revelation exposes the devastating, cruel irony of Matilda's entire adult life:</p><ul><li>Matilda lived a borrowed fantasy of wealth for just one night, only to ruin thirty years of her life in genuine, crushing poverty.</li><li>She threw away thirty-six thousand francs, her youth, beauty, and domestic happiness to replace a worthless piece of paste imitation jewelry worth a mere five hundred francs.</li><li>Her petty vanity and fear of confessing the loss to her friend turned a minor embarrassing incident into lifelong slavery, demonstrating how a single moment of false pride can destroy an entire life.</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Revelation: Original necklace was imitation glass/paste worth 500 francs</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Cruel situational irony: 10 years of brutal sacrifice wasted on worthless paste</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Moral critique of vanity, lack of honesty, and false bourgeois pride</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 26</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Value-Based Application</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How would the tragedy of Matilda's life have been averted if she had practiced honesty and frankness with Madame Forestier immediately after the ball?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>Had Matilda gathered moral courage to tell Madame Forestier the truth immediately, the friend would have instantly revealed that the necklace was a cheap five-hundred-franc imitation. The Loisels could have easily compensated her with a few days' salary without borrowing a single franc. False pride and the paralyzing fear of admitting loss ruined their lives, proving that honesty is not just a moral virtue, but a practical safeguard against catastrophe.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(25)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(27)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","27":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch27\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">27</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 8: Bholi</h2>\n      <p>K.A. Abbas — Female Literacy, Dignity & The Triumph Over Patriarchy — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why was Sulekha nicknamed 'Bholi' (the simpleton)? What physical and neurological misfortunes did she suffer in childhood?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When she was ten months old, Sulekha fell off a cot on her head, which damaged some part of her brain, leaving her mentally backward; hence everyone called her 'Bholi' (the simpleton). At two years old, an attack of smallpox left her entire body pockmarked, sparing only her eyes. Furthermore, she could not speak until she was five, and when she finally learned, she stammered heavily, prompting other children to mimic and mock her.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Head injury at 10 months damaged brain -> nicknamed 'Bholi' (simpleton)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Smallpox scars all over body at age 2 + severe stammering from age 5</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Why did Ramlal's wife agree to send Bholi to school, while refusing to send her other daughters?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>When the Tehsildar inaugurated the village primary school for girls, he ordered Numberdar Ramlal to set an example by sending his daughters. Ramlal's wife objected to sending Radha, Mangla, or Champa, fearing that nobody would marry educated girls. However, she readily agreed to send Bholi, arguing that with her ugly pockmarked face and lack of sense, she had zero chance of getting married anyway, so the school teachers could worry about her.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Tehsildar's mandate to village head Ramlal to send daughters to school</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mother's cynical calculation: No one will marry ugly, dull Bholi anyway</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How did Bholi's school teacher transform her from a terrified, stammering child into a confident student?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>While Bholi wept in a corner in terror, the teacher approached her with gentle, loving warmth—a tone Bholi had never heard in her family. When Bholi stammered <em>'Bh-Bh-Bholi'</em>, the teacher did not laugh, but affectionately encouraged her to complete her name. She gifted her a book with colorful pictures of birds and animals, reassuring Bholi that through education she would become more learned and respected than anyone in the village, and no one would ever dare laugh at her again.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Gentle, compassionate voice without ridicule or scolding</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Gifted picture book and assured her education would win her universal respect</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who was Bishamber Nath? Why did Bholi's parents agree to marry her to him?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Bishamber Nath was a prosperous, middle-aged grocer from another village with a big shop, his own house, and several thousand rupees in the bank. He was around fifty years old—the same age as Bholi's father—limped when he walked, and had grown-up children from a first marriage. Bholi's parents accepted his proposal because he did not ask for any dowry initially and lived far away, ignorant of Bholi's pockmarks and mental history.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Prosperous 50-year-old grocer with limp, big house, and grown-up children</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Parents agreed because he did not ask for dowry and was unaware of pockmarks</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What caused the crisis at the wedding ceremony? How did Bishamber blackmail Ramlal?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>At the garland ceremony, a woman slipped back Bholi's veil, revealing her face. Seeing her pockmarks, Bishamber stopped abruptly and refused to marry her unless Ramlal paid him a cash dowry of five thousand rupees on the spot. Desperate to save his family's honor, Ramlal wept and placed his turban at Bishamber's feet, finally handing over a bundle of five thousand rupees.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Bishamber saw pockmarks when veil slipped; refused garland</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Extorted 5,000 rupees dowry; Ramlal surrendered pride and paid cash</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_6\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_6')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q6</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">'Education is the supreme catalyst for female emancipation.' How did schooling transform Bholi into Sulekha, a woman of unshakeable courage and self-respect?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">6 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. From 'Mute Cow' to Independent Voice:</strong><br>Throughout childhood, Bholi was treated as a submissive, dispensable burden—a 'dumb cow' who stammered in fear. However, years of dedicated schooling ignited a quiet revolution inside her soul, nurturing intellect, self-worth, and moral discernment.</p><p><strong>2. The Climactic Act of Defiance:</strong><br>When Bishamber greedily raised the garland after extorting five thousand rupees, Bholi's hand struck out like lightning. She flung the wedding garland into the sacred fire, threw off her veil, and spoke in a clear, loud, steady voice with zero stammer. She firmly declared: <em>'Father! Take back your money. I am not going to marry this man!'</em></p><p><strong>3. Triumph of Sulekha:</strong><br>When old women mocked her as shameless, Bholi silenced them with dignified fire. She announced that to honor her father's age, she had agreed to marry a limping, elderly widower, but she would never accept a greedy, cowardly wretch as her husband. She promised to serve her parents in their old age and teach in the very school where she found her voice. Watching quietly from a corner, her smiling teacher witnessed the masterpiece she had sculpted—proving that education transforms voiceless victims into courageous sovereign women.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Internal transformation through years of schooling and teacher's love</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Rejection of dowry and greedy groom: Flung garland into sacred fire</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Sulekha's proud resolution to serve parents and teach in village school</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 27</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Social Critique & Gender Empowerment</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does 'Bholi' expose the deeply rooted evils of dowry, patriarchy, and superficial beauty standards in Indian society?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>K.A. Abbas delivers a trenchant critique of patriarchal social conditioning. Ramlal's household valued daughters solely as marriage commodities: fair and pretty daughters were married off easily, while Bholi was neglected due to skin scars. Bishamber viewed marriage as a commercial transaction, shameless in extorting money from a humiliated father. Bholi's rebellion shatters this feudal mindset, demonstrating that a woman's true beauty lies in self-respect, moral courage, and financial self-reliance.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(26)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn next\" onclick=\"showChapter(28)\">Next Unit →</button>\n  </div>\n</section>\n","28":"<section class=\"chapter-section\" id=\"ch28\" data-book=\"Footprints without Feet\">\n  <div class=\"chapter-header\">\n    <div class=\"ch-badge\">28</div>\n    <div class=\"chapter-header-info\">\n      <div class=\"ch-category\">FOOTPRINTS SUPPLEMENTARY</div>\n      <h2>Chapter 9: The Book That Saved the Earth</h2>\n      <p>Claire Boiko — Science-Fiction Comedy, Egotism & The Power of Books — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"ex-div\">I. Textbook Exercise Solutions & Important Questions — CBSE Marking Scheme 2026-27</div>\n\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_1\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_1')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q1</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">When is the play set, and what era does the Historian describe in the Museum of Ancient History?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The play is framed in the twenty-fifth century, where the Historian addresses visitors at the Department of Twenty-First Century in the Museum of Ancient History. She explains that the twentieth century was famously known as the <strong>'Era of the Book'</strong>—a time when books taught people everything from how to, when to, where to, and why to. The most remarkable book of all was a book of nursery rhymes that saved the Earth from a Martian invasion in 2040.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Setting: 25th century at Museum of Ancient History</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Era of the Book: 20th century, books taught everything; nursery rhyme saved Earth</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_2\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_2')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q2</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Who is Think-Tank? Describe his physical appearance and overbearing personality.</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>Think-Tank is the Supreme Commander of Mars Space Control. He is a pompous, arrogant, and absurdly vain ruler who has a huge, balloon-shaped egghead and wears a magnificent robe decorated with stars and circles. He demands to be saluted by his subordinates as <em>'Think-Tank, Great and Mighty, Commander-in-Chief, most powerful and intelligent creature in the whole universe'</em>, constantly admiring his reflection in a mirror.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Appearance: Huge balloon egghead, robes decorated with stars/circles</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Personality: Arrogant, boastful, demands elaborate flattery from subordinates</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_3\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_3')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q3</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">Where does the Martian probe crew land on Earth, and what do they mistake books for?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>The Martian crew—Captain Omega, Lieutenant Iota, and Sergeant Oop—lands inside the Centerville Public Library. Never having seen a book, they are completely baffled by the thousands of books on shelves. When they consult Think-Tank via video communication, Think-Tank makes three hilarious blunders:</p><ol><li>First, he identifies books as <strong>'sandwiches'</strong> (Earthling dietary staple).</li><li>Second, he identifies them as <strong>'communication sandwiches'</strong> for listening.</li><li>Third, he identifies them as <strong>'eye communication devices'</strong> for viewing.</li></ol>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Location: Centerville Public Library (baffled by shelves of books)</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Three blunders: Food sandwiches -> listening devices -> eye communication spectacles</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_4\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_4')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q4</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">What nursery rhymes does the Martian crew read from 'Mother Goose'? How does Think-Tank misinterpret them?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">3 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p>After taking chemical vitamins to decipher the printed codes of 'Mother Goose', the crew reads three rhymes:</p><ul><li><strong>'Mistress Mary':</strong> Mentions cockle shells and silver bells grown in gardens. Think-Tank panics, believing Earthlings have discovered how to combine agriculture and mining to grow rare metals and explosives.</li><li><strong>'Hey Diddle Diddle':</strong> The cow jumping over the moon makes him believe Earthlings have trained domesticated animals for interplanetary space warfare.</li><li><strong>'Humpty Dumpty':</strong> Seeing the picture of the egghead falling off the wall, Think-Tank is convinced Earthlings know him, have drawn his picture, and are plotting to topple his balloon head and conquer Mars!</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Mistress Mary: Interpreted as growing metal weapons and explosives in gardens</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Hey Diddle Diddle: Interpreted as animals trained for space combat</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Humpty Dumpty: Convinced Earthlings are targeting his own balloon-shaped head</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1 Mark</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"q-card\" id=\"fp8_5\">\n    <div class=\"q-head\" onclick=\"toggleQ('fp8_5')\">\n      <div class=\"q-num\">Q5</div>\n      <div class=\"q-text\">How does a simple nursery rhyme book save planet Earth from a Martian invasion? What does the play satirize?</div>\n      <div class=\"q-marks\">5 Marks</div>\n      <div class=\"q-toggle\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"5\" x2=\"12\" y2=\"19\"/><line x1=\"5\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"19\" y2=\"12\"/></svg></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"q-answer\">\n      <div class=\"answer-box\">\n        <div class=\"answer-label\">✅ CBSE Standard Answer (Max Word Count)</div>\n        <div class=\"answer-text\">\n<p><strong>1. The Panic and Flight:</strong><br>Terrified by the picture of Humpty Dumpty, Think-Tank orders Captain Omega and the crew to evacuate Earth immediately without leaving a trace. He orders his space fleet to prepare a capsule for his own escape to the planet Alpha Centauri, a hundred million miles away, to escape the 'terrifying' Earthlings. A humble children's book of nursery rhymes ('Mother Goose') successfully repelled a full-scale extraterrestrial invasion without firing a single weapon.</p><p><strong>2. Satire on Arrogance and Half-Knowledge:</strong><br>Claire Boiko's play is a delightful satire on imperialist arrogance and intellectual vanity. Think-Tank claims to be the most supreme intellect in the cosmos, yet his total ignorance of literature and context leads him to literal misinterpretation. The play demonstrates that literal thinking without contextual wisdom turns power into absurdity.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"marking-scheme\">\n          <div class=\"marking-title\">CBSE Marking Scheme Breakdown 2026-27</div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Think-Tank's panicked evacuation to Alpha Centauri due to Humpty Dumpty picture</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">2 Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Children's nursery book ('Mother Goose') averted cosmic invasion</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n          <div class=\"marking-row\"><span class=\"marking-key\">Satire: Arrogance, ignorance, half-baked knowledge leading to comical paranoia</span><span class=\"marking-marks\">1½ Marks</span></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"cbq-section\">\n    <div class=\"cbq-header\"><span>🎯 Competency-Based & Value-Based Questions — Unit 28</span><span class=\"cbq-badge\">CBSE 2026-27</span></div>\n    <div class=\"cbq-body\">\n      <div class=\"cbq-card\" style=\"border-left:4px solid #0284c7;\">\n        <div class=\"cbq-type\" style=\"color:#0284c7;\">Science Fiction & Satirical Analysis</div>\n        <div class=\"cbq-question\"><strong>Analysis:</strong> How does 'The Book That Saved the Earth' pay a creative tribute to the value of human libraries and cultural literacy?</div>\n        <button class=\"cbq-show-btn\" onclick=\"toggleCBQ(this)\">▶ Show Answer</button>\n        <div class=\"cbq-answer\"><p>The play celebrates libraries as the ultimate vaults of human civilization. The Martians possessed spaceships, vitamins for intelligence, and advanced communication transmitters, yet they were completely defenseless against human cultural imagination. Books contain poetry, metaphor, nursery humor, and emotional depth that technological algorithms and literalist invaders cannot decode, proving that reading literacy is humanity's greatest superpower.</p></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chapter-nav-btns\">\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"showChapter(27)\">← Previous Unit</button>\n    <button class=\"ch-nav-btn\" onclick=\"window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})\">↑ Back to Top</button>\n    <div></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n"};
